            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-12243",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "gnutls: GnuTLS Impacted by Inefficient DER Decoding in libtasn1 Leading to Remote DoS"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in GnuTLS, which relies on libtasn1 for ASN.1 data processing. Due to an inefficient algorithm in libtasn1, decoding certain DER-encoded certificate data can take excessive time, leading to increased resource consumption. This flaw allows a remote attacker to send a specially crafted certificate, causing GnuTLS to become unresponsive or slow, resulting in a denial-of-service condition."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-12243",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-12243\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libgnutls30t64\nFixed Version: 3.8.3-1.1ubuntu3.3\nLink: [CVE-2024-12243](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-12243)\nA flaw was found in GnuTLS, which relies on libtasn1 for ASN.1 data processing. Due to an inefficient algorithm in libtasn1, decoding certain DER-encoded certificate data can take excessive time, leading to increased resource consumption. This flaw allows a remote attacker to send a specially crafted certificate, causing GnuTLS to become unresponsive or slow, resulting in a denial-of-service condition.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-12243**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libgnutls30t64|3.8.3-1.1ubuntu3.3|[CVE-2024-12243](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-12243)|\n\nA flaw was found in GnuTLS, which relies on libtasn1 for ASN.1 data processing. Due to an inefficient algorithm in libtasn1, decoding certain DER-encoded certificate data can take excessive time, leading to increased resource consumption. This flaw allows a remote attacker to send a specially crafted certificate, causing GnuTLS to become unresponsive or slow, resulting in a denial-of-service condition."
