            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-4877",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "libssh: Write beyond bounds in binary to base64 conversion functions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "There's a vulnerability in the libssh package where when a libssh consumer passes in an unexpectedly large input buffer to ssh_get_fingerprint_hash() function. In such cases the bin_to_base64() function can experience an integer overflow leading to a memory under allocation, when that happens it's possible that the program perform out of bounds write leading to a heap corruption.\nThis issue affects only 32-bits builds of libssh."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-4877",
