            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-22036",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: exfat: fix random stack corruption after get_block"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nexfat: fix random stack corruption after get_block\n\nWhen get_block is called with a buffer_head allocated on the stack, such\nas do_mpage_readpage, stack corruption due to buffer_head UAF may occur in\nthe following race condition situation.\n\n     \u003cCPU 0\u003e                      \u003cCPU 1\u003e\nmpage_read_folio\n  \u003c\u003cbh on stack\u003e\u003e\n  do_mpage_readpage\n    exfat_get_block\n      bh_read\n        __bh_read\n\t  get_bh(bh)\n          submit_bh\n          wait_on_buffer\n                              ...\n                              end_buffer_read_sync\n                                __end_buffer_read_notouch\n                                   unlock_buffer\n          \u003c\u003ckeep going\u003e\u003e\n        ...\n      ...\n    ...\n  ...\n\u003c\u003cbh is not valid out of mpage_read_folio\u003e\u003e\n   .\n   .\nanother_function\n  \u003c\u003cvariable A on stack\u003e\u003e\n                                   put_bh(bh)\n                                     atomic_dec(bh-\u003eb_count)\n  * stack corruption here *\n\nThis patch returns -EAGAIN if a folio does not have buffers when bh_read\nneeds to be called. By doing this, the caller can fallback to functions\nlike block_read_full_folio(), create a buffer_head in the folio, and then\ncall get_block again.\n\nLet's do not call bh_read() with on-stack buffer_head."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22036",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-22036\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-86.87\nLink: [CVE-2025-22036](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22036)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nexfat: fix random stack corruption after get_block\n\nWhen get_block is called with a buffer_head allocated on the stack, such\nas do_mpage_readpage, stack corruption due to buffer_head UAF may occur in\nthe following race condition situation.\n\n     \u003cCPU 0\u003e                      \u003cCPU 1\u003e\nmpage_read_folio\n  \u003c\u003cbh on stack\u003e\u003e\n  do_mpage_readpage\n    exfat_get_block\n      bh_read\n        __bh_read\n\t  get_bh(bh)\n          submit_bh\n          wait_on_buffer\n                              ...\n                              end_buffer_read_sync\n                                __end_buffer_read_notouch\n                                   unlock_buffer\n          \u003c\u003ckeep going\u003e\u003e\n        ...\n      ...\n    ...\n  ...\n\u003c\u003cbh is not valid out of mpage_read_folio\u003e\u003e\n   .\n   .\nanother_function\n  \u003c\u003cvariable A on stack\u003e\u003e\n                                   put_bh(bh)\n                                     atomic_dec(bh-\u003eb_count)\n  * stack corruption here *\n\nThis patch returns -EAGAIN if a folio does not have buffers when bh_read\nneeds to be called. By doing this, the caller can fallback to functions\nlike block_read_full_folio(), create a buffer_head in the folio, and then\ncall get_block again.\n\nLet's do not call bh_read() with on-stack buffer_head.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-22036**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-86.87|[CVE-2025-22036](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22036)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nexfat: fix random stack corruption after get_block\n\nWhen get_block is called with a buffer_head allocated on the stack, such\nas do_mpage_readpage, stack corruption due to buffer_head UAF may occur in\nthe following race condition situation.\n\n     \u003cCPU 0\u003e                      \u003cCPU 1\u003e\nmpage_read_folio\n  \u003c\u003cbh on stack\u003e\u003e\n  do_mpage_readpage\n    exfat_get_block\n      bh_read\n        __bh_read\n\t  get_bh(bh)\n          submit_bh\n          wait_on_buffer\n                              ...\n                              end_buffer_read_sync\n                                __end_buffer_read_notouch\n                                   unlock_buffer\n          \u003c\u003ckeep going\u003e\u003e\n        ...\n      ...\n    ...\n  ...\n\u003c\u003cbh is not valid out of mpage_read_folio\u003e\u003e\n   .\n   .\nanother_function\n  \u003c\u003cvariable A on stack\u003e\u003e\n                                   put_bh(bh)\n                                     atomic_dec(bh-\u003eb_count)\n  * stack corruption here *\n\nThis patch returns -EAGAIN if a folio does not have buffers when bh_read\nneeds to be called. By doing this, the caller can fallback to functions\nlike block_read_full_folio(), create a buffer_head in the folio, and then\ncall get_block again.\n\nLet's do not call bh_read() with on-stack buffer_head."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-22088",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: RDMA/erdma: Prevent use-after-free in erdma_accept_newconn()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/erdma: Prevent use-after-free in erdma_accept_newconn()\n\nAfter the erdma_cep_put(new_cep) being called, new_cep will be freed,\nand the following dereference will cause a UAF problem. Fix this issue."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22088",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-22088\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-63.66\nLink: [CVE-2025-22088](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22088)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/erdma: Prevent use-after-free in erdma_accept_newconn()\n\nAfter the erdma_cep_put(new_cep) being called, new_cep will be freed,\nand the following dereference will cause a UAF problem. Fix this issue.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-22088**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-63.66|[CVE-2025-22088](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22088)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/erdma: Prevent use-after-free in erdma_accept_newconn()\n\nAfter the erdma_cep_put(new_cep) being called, new_cep will be freed,\nand the following dereference will cause a UAF problem. Fix this issue."
              },
