              "id": "CVE-2024-36347",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: hw:amd: Improper signature verification in AMD CPU ROM microcode patch loader"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Improper signature verification in AMD CPU ROM microcode patch loader may allow an attacker with local administrator privilege to load malicious microcode, potentially resulting in loss of integrity of x86 instruction execution, loss of confidentiality and integrity of data in x86 CPU privileged context and compromise of SMM execution environment."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-36347",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-36347\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-84.84\nLink: [CVE-2024-36347](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-36347)\nImproper signature verification in AMD CPU ROM microcode patch loader may allow an attacker with local administrator privilege to load malicious microcode, potentially resulting in loss of integrity of x86 instruction execution, loss of confidentiality and integrity of data in x86 CPU privileged context and compromise of SMM execution environment.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-36347**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-84.84|[CVE-2024-36347](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-36347)|\n\nImproper signature verification in AMD CPU ROM microcode patch loader may allow an attacker with local administrator privilege to load malicious microcode, potentially resulting in loss of integrity of x86 instruction execution, loss of confidentiality and integrity of data in x86 CPU privileged context and compromise of SMM execution environment."
