            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-48876",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: stackdepot: fix stack_depot_save_flags() in NMI context"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nstackdepot: fix stack_depot_save_flags() in NMI context\n\nPer documentation, stack_depot_save_flags() was meant to be usable from\nNMI context if STACK_DEPOT_FLAG_CAN_ALLOC is unset.  However, it still\nwould try to take the pool_lock in an attempt to save a stack trace in the\ncurrent pool (if space is available).\n\nThis could result in deadlock if an NMI is handled while pool_lock is\nalready held.  To avoid deadlock, only try to take the lock in NMI context\nand give up if unsuccessful.\n\nThe documentation is fixed to clearly convey this."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-48876",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-48876\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-48876](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-48876)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nstackdepot: fix stack_depot_save_flags() in NMI context\n\nPer documentation, stack_depot_save_flags() was meant to be usable from\nNMI context if STACK_DEPOT_FLAG_CAN_ALLOC is unset.  However, it still\nwould try to take the pool_lock in an attempt to save a stack trace in the\ncurrent pool (if space is available).\n\nThis could result in deadlock if an NMI is handled while pool_lock is\nalready held.  To avoid deadlock, only try to take the lock in NMI context\nand give up if unsuccessful.\n\nThe documentation is fixed to clearly convey this.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-48876**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-48876](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-48876)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nstackdepot: fix stack_depot_save_flags() in NMI context\n\nPer documentation, stack_depot_save_flags() was meant to be usable from\nNMI context if STACK_DEPOT_FLAG_CAN_ALLOC is unset.  However, it still\nwould try to take the pool_lock in an attempt to save a stack trace in the\ncurrent pool (if space is available).\n\nThis could result in deadlock if an NMI is handled while pool_lock is\nalready held.  To avoid deadlock, only try to take the lock in NMI context\nand give up if unsuccessful.\n\nThe documentation is fixed to clearly convey this."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-48881",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: bcache: revert replacing IS_ERR_OR_NULL with IS_ERR again"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbcache: revert replacing IS_ERR_OR_NULL with IS_ERR again\n\nCommit 028ddcac477b (\"bcache: Remove unnecessary NULL point check in\nnode allocations\") leads a NULL pointer deference in cache_set_flush().\n\n1721         if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(c-\u003eroot))\n1722                 list_add(\u0026c-\u003eroot-\u003elist, \u0026c-\u003ebtree_cache);\n\n\u003eFrom the above code in cache_set_flush(), if previous registration code\nfails before allocating c-\u003eroot, it is possible c-\u003eroot is NULL as what\nit is initialized. __bch_btree_node_alloc() never returns NULL but\nc-\u003eroot is possible to be NULL at above line 1721.\n\nThis patch replaces IS_ERR() by IS_ERR_OR_NULL() to fix this."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-48881",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-48881\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-48881](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-48881)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbcache: revert replacing IS_ERR_OR_NULL with IS_ERR again\n\nCommit 028ddcac477b (\"bcache: Remove unnecessary NULL point check in\nnode allocations\") leads a NULL pointer deference in cache_set_flush().\n\n1721         if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(c-\u003eroot))\n1722                 list_add(\u0026c-\u003eroot-\u003elist, \u0026c-\u003ebtree_cache);\n\n\u003eFrom the above code in cache_set_flush(), if previous registration code\nfails before allocating c-\u003eroot, it is possible c-\u003eroot is NULL as what\nit is initialized. __bch_btree_node_alloc() never returns NULL but\nc-\u003eroot is possible to be NULL at above line 1721.\n\nThis patch replaces IS_ERR() by IS_ERR_OR_NULL() to fix this.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-48881**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-48881](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-48881)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbcache: revert replacing IS_ERR_OR_NULL with IS_ERR again\n\nCommit 028ddcac477b (\"bcache: Remove unnecessary NULL point check in\nnode allocations\") leads a NULL pointer deference in cache_set_flush().\n\n1721         if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(c-\u003eroot))\n1722                 list_add(\u0026c-\u003eroot-\u003elist, \u0026c-\u003ebtree_cache);\n\n\u003eFrom the above code in cache_set_flush(), if previous registration code\nfails before allocating c-\u003eroot, it is possible c-\u003eroot is NULL as what\nit is initialized. __bch_btree_node_alloc() never returns NULL but\nc-\u003eroot is possible to be NULL at above line 1721.\n\nThis patch replaces IS_ERR() by IS_ERR_OR_NULL() to fix this."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-49568",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: net/smc: check v2_ext_offset/eid_cnt/ism_gid_cnt when receiving proposal msg"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/smc: check v2_ext_offset/eid_cnt/ism_gid_cnt when receiving proposal msg\n\nWhen receiving proposal msg in server, the fields v2_ext_offset/\neid_cnt/ism_gid_cnt in proposal msg are from the remote client\nand can not be fully trusted. Especially the field v2_ext_offset,\nonce exceed the max value, there has the chance to access wrong\naddress, and crash may happen.\n\nThis patch checks the fields v2_ext_offset/eid_cnt/ism_gid_cnt\nbefore using them."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-49568",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-49568\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-60.63\nLink: [CVE-2024-49568](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-49568)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/smc: check v2_ext_offset/eid_cnt/ism_gid_cnt when receiving proposal msg\n\nWhen receiving proposal msg in server, the fields v2_ext_offset/\neid_cnt/ism_gid_cnt in proposal msg are from the remote client\nand can not be fully trusted. Especially the field v2_ext_offset,\nonce exceed the max value, there has the chance to access wrong\naddress, and crash may happen.\n\nThis patch checks the fields v2_ext_offset/eid_cnt/ism_gid_cnt\nbefore using them.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-49568**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-60.63|[CVE-2024-49568](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-49568)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/smc: check v2_ext_offset/eid_cnt/ism_gid_cnt when receiving proposal msg\n\nWhen receiving proposal msg in server, the fields v2_ext_offset/\neid_cnt/ism_gid_cnt in proposal msg are from the remote client\nand can not be fully trusted. Especially the field v2_ext_offset,\nonce exceed the max value, there has the chance to access wrong\naddress, and crash may happen.\n\nThis patch checks the fields v2_ext_offset/eid_cnt/ism_gid_cnt\nbefore using them."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-49569",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: nvme-rdma: unquiesce admin_q before destroy it"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvme-rdma: unquiesce admin_q before destroy it\n\nKernel will hang on destroy admin_q while we create ctrl failed, such\nas following calltrace:\n\nPID: 23644    TASK: ff2d52b40f439fc0  CPU: 2    COMMAND: \"nvme\"\n #0 [ff61d23de260fb78] __schedule at ffffffff8323bc15\n #1 [ff61d23de260fc08] schedule at ffffffff8323c014\n #2 [ff61d23de260fc28] blk_mq_freeze_queue_wait at ffffffff82a3dba1\n #3 [ff61d23de260fc78] blk_freeze_queue at ffffffff82a4113a\n #4 [ff61d23de260fc90] blk_cleanup_queue at ffffffff82a33006\n #5 [ff61d23de260fcb0] nvme_rdma_destroy_admin_queue at ffffffffc12686ce\n #6 [ff61d23de260fcc8] nvme_rdma_setup_ctrl at ffffffffc1268ced\n #7 [ff61d23de260fd28] nvme_rdma_create_ctrl at ffffffffc126919b\n #8 [ff61d23de260fd68] nvmf_dev_write at ffffffffc024f362\n #9 [ff61d23de260fe38] vfs_write at ffffffff827d5f25\n    RIP: 00007fda7891d574  RSP: 00007ffe2ef06958  RFLAGS: 00000202\n    RAX: ffffffffffffffda  RBX: 000055e8122a4d90  RCX: 00007fda7891d574\n    RDX: 000000000000012b  RSI: 000055e8122a4d90  RDI: 0000000000000004\n    RBP: 00007ffe2ef079c0   R8: 000000000000012b   R9: 000055e8122a4d90\n    R10: 0000000000000000  R11: 0000000000000202  R12: 0000000000000004\n    R13: 000055e8122923c0  R14: 000000000000012b  R15: 00007fda78a54500\n    ORIG_RAX: 0000000000000001  CS: 0033  SS: 002b\n\nThis due to we have quiesced admi_q before cancel requests, but forgot\nto unquiesce before destroy it, as a result we fail to drain the\npending requests, and hang on blk_mq_freeze_queue_wait() forever. Here\ntry to reuse nvme_rdma_teardown_admin_queue() to fix this issue and\nsimplify the code."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-49569",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-49569\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-49569](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-49569)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvme-rdma: unquiesce admin_q before destroy it\n\nKernel will hang on destroy admin_q while we create ctrl failed, such\nas following calltrace:\n\nPID: 23644    TASK: ff2d52b40f439fc0  CPU: 2    COMMAND: \"nvme\"\n #0 [ff61d23de260fb78] __schedule at ffffffff8323bc15\n #1 [ff61d23de260fc08] schedule at ffffffff8323c014\n #2 [ff61d23de260fc28] blk_mq_freeze_queue_wait at ffffffff82a3dba1\n #3 [ff61d23de260fc78] blk_freeze_queue at ffffffff82a4113a\n #4 [ff61d23de260fc90] blk_cleanup_queue at ffffffff82a33006\n #5 [ff61d23de260fcb0] nvme_rdma_destroy_admin_queue at ffffffffc12686ce\n #6 [ff61d23de260fcc8] nvme_rdma_setup_ctrl at ffffffffc1268ced\n #7 [ff61d23de260fd28] nvme_rdma_create_ctrl at ffffffffc126919b\n #8 [ff61d23de260fd68] nvmf_dev_write at ffffffffc024f362\n #9 [ff61d23de260fe38] vfs_write at ffffffff827d5f25\n    RIP: 00007fda7891d574  RSP: 00007ffe2ef06958  RFLAGS: 00000202\n    RAX: ffffffffffffffda  RBX: 000055e8122a4d90  RCX: 00007fda7891d574\n    RDX: 000000000000012b  RSI: 000055e8122a4d90  RDI: 0000000000000004\n    RBP: 00007ffe2ef079c0   R8: 000000000000012b   R9: 000055e8122a4d90\n    R10: 0000000000000000  R11: 0000000000000202  R12: 0000000000000004\n    R13: 000055e8122923c0  R14: 000000000000012b  R15: 00007fda78a54500\n    ORIG_RAX: 0000000000000001  CS: 0033  SS: 002b\n\nThis due to we have quiesced admi_q before cancel requests, but forgot\nto unquiesce before destroy it, as a result we fail to drain the\npending requests, and hang on blk_mq_freeze_queue_wait() forever. Here\ntry to reuse nvme_rdma_teardown_admin_queue() to fix this issue and\nsimplify the code.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-49569**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-49569](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-49569)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvme-rdma: unquiesce admin_q before destroy it\n\nKernel will hang on destroy admin_q while we create ctrl failed, such\nas following calltrace:\n\nPID: 23644    TASK: ff2d52b40f439fc0  CPU: 2    COMMAND: \"nvme\"\n #0 [ff61d23de260fb78] __schedule at ffffffff8323bc15\n #1 [ff61d23de260fc08] schedule at ffffffff8323c014\n #2 [ff61d23de260fc28] blk_mq_freeze_queue_wait at ffffffff82a3dba1\n #3 [ff61d23de260fc78] blk_freeze_queue at ffffffff82a4113a\n #4 [ff61d23de260fc90] blk_cleanup_queue at ffffffff82a33006\n #5 [ff61d23de260fcb0] nvme_rdma_destroy_admin_queue at ffffffffc12686ce\n #6 [ff61d23de260fcc8] nvme_rdma_setup_ctrl at ffffffffc1268ced\n #7 [ff61d23de260fd28] nvme_rdma_create_ctrl at ffffffffc126919b\n #8 [ff61d23de260fd68] nvmf_dev_write at ffffffffc024f362\n #9 [ff61d23de260fe38] vfs_write at ffffffff827d5f25\n    RIP: 00007fda7891d574  RSP: 00007ffe2ef06958  RFLAGS: 00000202\n    RAX: ffffffffffffffda  RBX: 000055e8122a4d90  RCX: 00007fda7891d574\n    RDX: 000000000000012b  RSI: 000055e8122a4d90  RDI: 0000000000000004\n    RBP: 00007ffe2ef079c0   R8: 000000000000012b   R9: 000055e8122a4d90\n    R10: 0000000000000000  R11: 0000000000000202  R12: 0000000000000004\n    R13: 000055e8122923c0  R14: 000000000000012b  R15: 00007fda78a54500\n    ORIG_RAX: 0000000000000001  CS: 0033  SS: 002b\n\nThis due to we have quiesced admi_q before cancel requests, but forgot\nto unquiesce before destroy it, as a result we fail to drain the\npending requests, and hang on blk_mq_freeze_queue_wait() forever. Here\ntry to reuse nvme_rdma_teardown_admin_queue() to fix this issue and\nsimplify the code."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-49571",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: net/smc: check iparea_offset and ipv6_prefixes_cnt when receiving proposal msg"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/smc: check iparea_offset and ipv6_prefixes_cnt when receiving proposal msg\n\nWhen receiving proposal msg in server, the field iparea_offset\nand the field ipv6_prefixes_cnt in proposal msg are from the\nremote client and can not be fully trusted. Especially the\nfield iparea_offset, once exceed the max value, there has the\nchance to access wrong address, and crash may happen.\n\nThis patch checks iparea_offset and ipv6_prefixes_cnt before using them."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-49571",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-49571\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-60.63\nLink: [CVE-2024-49571](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-49571)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/smc: check iparea_offset and ipv6_prefixes_cnt when receiving proposal msg\n\nWhen receiving proposal msg in server, the field iparea_offset\nand the field ipv6_prefixes_cnt in proposal msg are from the\nremote client and can not be fully trusted. Especially the\nfield iparea_offset, once exceed the max value, there has the\nchance to access wrong address, and crash may happen.\n\nThis patch checks iparea_offset and ipv6_prefixes_cnt before using them.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-49571**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-60.63|[CVE-2024-49571](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-49571)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/smc: check iparea_offset and ipv6_prefixes_cnt when receiving proposal msg\n\nWhen receiving proposal msg in server, the field iparea_offset\nand the field ipv6_prefixes_cnt in proposal msg are from the\nremote client and can not be fully trusted. Especially the\nfield iparea_offset, once exceed the max value, there has the\nchance to access wrong address, and crash may happen.\n\nThis patch checks iparea_offset and ipv6_prefixes_cnt before using them."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
