            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-49972",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/amd/display: Deallocate DML memory if allocation fails"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Deallocate DML memory if allocation fails\n\n[Why]\nWhen DC state create DML memory allocation fails, memory is not\ndeallocated subsequently, resulting in uninitialized structure\nthat is not NULL.\n\n[How]\nDeallocate memory if DML memory allocation fails."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-49972",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-49972\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-56.58\nLink: [CVE-2024-49972](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-49972)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Deallocate DML memory if allocation fails\n\n[Why]\nWhen DC state create DML memory allocation fails, memory is not\ndeallocated subsequently, resulting in uninitialized structure\nthat is not NULL.\n\n[How]\nDeallocate memory if DML memory allocation fails.",
