            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50028",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: thermal: core: Reference count the zone in thermal_zone_get_by_id()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nthermal: core: Reference count the zone in thermal_zone_get_by_id()\n\nThere are places in the thermal netlink code where nothing prevents\nthe thermal zone object from going away while being accessed after it\nhas been returned by thermal_zone_get_by_id().\n\nTo address this, make thermal_zone_get_by_id() get a reference on the\nthermal zone device object to be returned with the help of get_device(),\nunder thermal_list_lock, and adjust all of its callers to this change\nwith the help of the cleanup.h infrastructure."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50028",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50028\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-56.58\nLink: [CVE-2024-50028](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50028)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nthermal: core: Reference count the zone in thermal_zone_get_by_id()\n\nThere are places in the thermal netlink code where nothing prevents\nthe thermal zone object from going away while being accessed after it\nhas been returned by thermal_zone_get_by_id().\n\nTo address this, make thermal_zone_get_by_id() get a reference on the\nthermal zone device object to be returned with the help of get_device(),\nunder thermal_list_lock, and adjust all of its callers to this change\nwith the help of the cleanup.h infrastructure.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50028**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-56.58|[CVE-2024-50028](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50028)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nthermal: core: Reference count the zone in thermal_zone_get_by_id()\n\nThere are places in the thermal netlink code where nothing prevents\nthe thermal zone object from going away while being accessed after it\nhas been returned by thermal_zone_get_by_id().\n\nTo address this, make thermal_zone_get_by_id() get a reference on the\nthermal zone device object to be returned with the help of get_device(),\nunder thermal_list_lock, and adjust all of its callers to this change\nwith the help of the cleanup.h infrastructure."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
