            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50051",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: spi: mpc52xx: Add cancel_work_sync before module remove"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nspi: mpc52xx: Add cancel_work_sync before module remove\n\nIf we remove the module which will call mpc52xx_spi_remove\nit will free 'ms' through spi_unregister_controller.\nwhile the work ms-\u003ework will be used. The sequence of operations\nthat may lead to a UAF bug.\n\nFix it by ensuring that the work is canceled before proceeding with\nthe cleanup in mpc52xx_spi_remove."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50051",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50051\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-50051](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50051)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nspi: mpc52xx: Add cancel_work_sync before module remove\n\nIf we remove the module which will call mpc52xx_spi_remove\nit will free 'ms' through spi_unregister_controller.\nwhile the work ms-\u003ework will be used. The sequence of operations\nthat may lead to a UAF bug.\n\nFix it by ensuring that the work is canceled before proceeding with\nthe cleanup in mpc52xx_spi_remove.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50051**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-50051](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50051)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nspi: mpc52xx: Add cancel_work_sync before module remove\n\nIf we remove the module which will call mpc52xx_spi_remove\nit will free 'ms' through spi_unregister_controller.\nwhile the work ms-\u003ework will be used. The sequence of operations\nthat may lead to a UAF bug.\n\nFix it by ensuring that the work is canceled before proceeding with\nthe cleanup in mpc52xx_spi_remove."
              },
