            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50065",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ntfs3: Change to non-blocking allocation in ntfs_d_hash"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nntfs3: Change to non-blocking allocation in ntfs_d_hash\n\nd_hash is done while under \"rcu-walk\" and should not sleep.\n__get_name() allocates using GFP_KERNEL, having the possibility\nto sleep when under memory pressure. Change the allocation to\nGFP_NOWAIT."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50065",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50065\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-56.58\nLink: [CVE-2024-50065](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50065)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nntfs3: Change to non-blocking allocation in ntfs_d_hash\n\nd_hash is done while under \"rcu-walk\" and should not sleep.\n__get_name() allocates using GFP_KERNEL, having the possibility\nto sleep when under memory pressure. Change the allocation to\nGFP_NOWAIT.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50065**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-56.58|[CVE-2024-50065](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50065)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nntfs3: Change to non-blocking allocation in ntfs_d_hash\n\nd_hash is done while under \"rcu-walk\" and should not sleep.\n__get_name() allocates using GFP_KERNEL, having the possibility\nto sleep when under memory pressure. Change the allocation to\nGFP_NOWAIT."
              },
