              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50070\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-56.58\nLink: [CVE-2024-50070](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50070)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npinctrl: stm32: check devm_kasprintf() returned value\n\ndevm_kasprintf() can return a NULL pointer on failure but this returned\nvalue is not checked. Fix this lack and check the returned value.\n\nFound by code review.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50070**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-56.58|[CVE-2024-50070](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50070)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npinctrl: stm32: check devm_kasprintf() returned value\n\ndevm_kasprintf() can return a NULL pointer on failure but this returned\nvalue is not checked. Fix this lack and check the returned value.\n\nFound by code review."
