            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50074",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: parport: Proper fix for array out-of-bounds access"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nparport: Proper fix for array out-of-bounds access\n\nThe recent fix for array out-of-bounds accesses replaced sprintf()\ncalls blindly with snprintf().  However, since snprintf() returns the\nwould-be-printed size, not the actually output size, the length\ncalculation can still go over the given limit.\n\nUse scnprintf() instead of snprintf(), which returns the actually\noutput letters, for addressing the potential out-of-bounds access\nproperly."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50074",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50074\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-56.58\nLink: [CVE-2024-50074](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50074)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nparport: Proper fix for array out-of-bounds access\n\nThe recent fix for array out-of-bounds accesses replaced sprintf()\ncalls blindly with snprintf().  However, since snprintf() returns the\nwould-be-printed size, not the actually output size, the length\ncalculation can still go over the given limit.\n\nUse scnprintf() instead of snprintf(), which returns the actually\noutput letters, for addressing the potential out-of-bounds access\nproperly.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50074**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-56.58|[CVE-2024-50074](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50074)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nparport: Proper fix for array out-of-bounds access\n\nThe recent fix for array out-of-bounds accesses replaced sprintf()\ncalls blindly with snprintf().  However, since snprintf() returns the\nwould-be-printed size, not the actually output size, the length\ncalculation can still go over the given limit.\n\nUse scnprintf() instead of snprintf(), which returns the actually\noutput letters, for addressing the potential out-of-bounds access\nproperly."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
