            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50108",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/amd/display: Disable PSR-SU on Parade 08-01 TCON too"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Disable PSR-SU on Parade 08-01 TCON too\n\nStuart Hayhurst has found that both at bootup and fullscreen VA-API video\nis leading to black screens for around 1 second and kernel WARNING [1] traces\nwhen calling dmub_psr_enable() with Parade 08-01 TCON.\n\nThese symptoms all go away with PSR-SU disabled for this TCON, so disable\nit for now while DMUB traces [2] from the failure can be analyzed and the failure\nstate properly root caused.\n\n(cherry picked from commit afb634a6823d8d9db23c5fb04f79c5549349628b)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50108",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50108\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-50108](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50108)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Disable PSR-SU on Parade 08-01 TCON too\n\nStuart Hayhurst has found that both at bootup and fullscreen VA-API video\nis leading to black screens for around 1 second and kernel WARNING [1] traces\nwhen calling dmub_psr_enable() with Parade 08-01 TCON.\n\nThese symptoms all go away with PSR-SU disabled for this TCON, so disable\nit for now while DMUB traces [2] from the failure can be analyzed and the failure\nstate properly root caused.\n\n(cherry picked from commit afb634a6823d8d9db23c5fb04f79c5549349628b)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50108**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-50108](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50108)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Disable PSR-SU on Parade 08-01 TCON too\n\nStuart Hayhurst has found that both at bootup and fullscreen VA-API video\nis leading to black screens for around 1 second and kernel WARNING [1] traces\nwhen calling dmub_psr_enable() with Parade 08-01 TCON.\n\nThese symptoms all go away with PSR-SU disabled for this TCON, so disable\nit for now while DMUB traces [2] from the failure can be analyzed and the failure\nstate properly root caused.\n\n(cherry picked from commit afb634a6823d8d9db23c5fb04f79c5549349628b)"
              },
