            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50130",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: netfilter: bpf: must hold reference on net namespace"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: bpf: must hold reference on net namespace\n\nBUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in __nf_unregister_net_hook+0x640/0x6b0\nRead of size 8 at addr ffff8880106fe400 by task repro/72=\nbpf_nf_link_release+0xda/0x1e0\nbpf_link_free+0x139/0x2d0\nbpf_link_release+0x68/0x80\n__fput+0x414/0xb60\n\nEric says:\n It seems that bpf was able to defer the __nf_unregister_net_hook()\n after exit()/close() time.\n Perhaps a netns reference is missing, because the netns has been\n dismantled/freed already.\n bpf_nf_link_attach() does :\n link-\u003enet = net;\n But I do not see a reference being taken on net.\n\nAdd such a reference and release it after hook unreg.\nNote that I was unable to get syzbot reproducer to work, so I\ndo not know if this resolves this splat."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50130",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50130\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-50130](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50130)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: bpf: must hold reference on net namespace\n\nBUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in __nf_unregister_net_hook+0x640/0x6b0\nRead of size 8 at addr ffff8880106fe400 by task repro/72=\nbpf_nf_link_release+0xda/0x1e0\nbpf_link_free+0x139/0x2d0\nbpf_link_release+0x68/0x80\n__fput+0x414/0xb60\n\nEric says:\n It seems that bpf was able to defer the __nf_unregister_net_hook()\n after exit()/close() time.\n Perhaps a netns reference is missing, because the netns has been\n dismantled/freed already.\n bpf_nf_link_attach() does :\n link-\u003enet = net;\n But I do not see a reference being taken on net.\n\nAdd such a reference and release it after hook unreg.\nNote that I was unable to get syzbot reproducer to work, so I\ndo not know if this resolves this splat.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50130**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-50130](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50130)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: bpf: must hold reference on net namespace\n\nBUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in __nf_unregister_net_hook+0x640/0x6b0\nRead of size 8 at addr ffff8880106fe400 by task repro/72=\nbpf_nf_link_release+0xda/0x1e0\nbpf_link_free+0x139/0x2d0\nbpf_link_release+0x68/0x80\n__fput+0x414/0xb60\n\nEric says:\n It seems that bpf was able to defer the __nf_unregister_net_hook()\n after exit()/close() time.\n Perhaps a netns reference is missing, because the netns has been\n dismantled/freed already.\n bpf_nf_link_attach() does :\n link-\u003enet = net;\n But I do not see a reference being taken on net.\n\nAdd such a reference and release it after hook unreg.\nNote that I was unable to get syzbot reproducer to work, so I\ndo not know if this resolves this splat."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50131",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: tracing: Consider the NULL character when validating the event length"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing: Consider the NULL character when validating the event length\n\nstrlen() returns a string length excluding the null byte. If the string\nlength equals to the maximum buffer length, the buffer will have no\nspace for the NULL terminating character.\n\nThis commit checks this condition and returns failure for it."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50131",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50131\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-50131](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50131)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing: Consider the NULL character when validating the event length\n\nstrlen() returns a string length excluding the null byte. If the string\nlength equals to the maximum buffer length, the buffer will have no\nspace for the NULL terminating character.\n\nThis commit checks this condition and returns failure for it.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50131**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-50131](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50131)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing: Consider the NULL character when validating the event length\n\nstrlen() returns a string length excluding the null byte. If the string\nlength equals to the maximum buffer length, the buffer will have no\nspace for the NULL terminating character.\n\nThis commit checks this condition and returns failure for it."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
