            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50166",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: fsl/fman: Fix refcount handling of fman-related devices"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfsl/fman: Fix refcount handling of fman-related devices\n\nIn mac_probe() there are multiple calls to of_find_device_by_node(),\nfman_bind() and fman_port_bind() which takes references to of_dev-\u003edev.\nNot all references taken by these calls are released later on error path\nin mac_probe() and in mac_remove() which lead to reference leaks.\n\nAdd references release."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50166",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50166\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-50166](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50166)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfsl/fman: Fix refcount handling of fman-related devices\n\nIn mac_probe() there are multiple calls to of_find_device_by_node(),\nfman_bind() and fman_port_bind() which takes references to of_dev-\u003edev.\nNot all references taken by these calls are released later on error path\nin mac_probe() and in mac_remove() which lead to reference leaks.\n\nAdd references release.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50166**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-50166](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50166)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfsl/fman: Fix refcount handling of fman-related devices\n\nIn mac_probe() there are multiple calls to of_find_device_by_node(),\nfman_bind() and fman_port_bind() which takes references to of_dev-\u003edev.\nNot all references taken by these calls are released later on error path\nin mac_probe() and in mac_remove() which lead to reference leaks.\n\nAdd references release."
