            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50169",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: vsock: Update rx_bytes on read_skb()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvsock: Update rx_bytes on read_skb()\n\nMake sure virtio_transport_inc_rx_pkt() and virtio_transport_dec_rx_pkt()\ncalls are balanced (i.e. virtio_vsock_sock::rx_bytes doesn't lie) after\nvsock_transport::read_skb().\n\nWhile here, also inform the peer that we've freed up space and it has more\ncredit.\n\nFailing to update rx_bytes after packet is dequeued leads to a warning on\nSOCK_STREAM recv():\n\n[  233.396654] rx_queue is empty, but rx_bytes is non-zero\n[  233.396702] WARNING: CPU: 11 PID: 40601 at net/vmw_vsock/virtio_transport_common.c:589"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50169",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50169\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-50169](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50169)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvsock: Update rx_bytes on read_skb()\n\nMake sure virtio_transport_inc_rx_pkt() and virtio_transport_dec_rx_pkt()\ncalls are balanced (i.e. virtio_vsock_sock::rx_bytes doesn't lie) after\nvsock_transport::read_skb().\n\nWhile here, also inform the peer that we've freed up space and it has more\ncredit.\n\nFailing to update rx_bytes after packet is dequeued leads to a warning on\nSOCK_STREAM recv():\n\n[  233.396654] rx_queue is empty, but rx_bytes is non-zero\n[  233.396702] WARNING: CPU: 11 PID: 40601 at net/vmw_vsock/virtio_transport_common.c:589",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50169**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-50169](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50169)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvsock: Update rx_bytes on read_skb()\n\nMake sure virtio_transport_inc_rx_pkt() and virtio_transport_dec_rx_pkt()\ncalls are balanced (i.e. virtio_vsock_sock::rx_bytes doesn't lie) after\nvsock_transport::read_skb().\n\nWhile here, also inform the peer that we've freed up space and it has more\ncredit.\n\nFailing to update rx_bytes after packet is dequeued leads to a warning on\nSOCK_STREAM recv():\n\n[  233.396654] rx_queue is empty, but rx_bytes is non-zero\n[  233.396702] WARNING: CPU: 11 PID: 40601 at net/vmw_vsock/virtio_transport_common.c:589"
              },
