            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50218",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ocfs2: pass u64 to ocfs2_truncate_inline maybe overflow"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nocfs2: pass u64 to ocfs2_truncate_inline maybe overflow\n\nSyzbot reported a kernel BUG in ocfs2_truncate_inline.  There are two\nreasons for this: first, the parameter value passed is greater than\nocfs2_max_inline_data_with_xattr, second, the start and end parameters of\nocfs2_truncate_inline are \"unsigned int\".\n\nSo, we need to add a sanity check for byte_start and byte_len right before\nocfs2_truncate_inline() in ocfs2_remove_inode_range(), if they are greater\nthan ocfs2_max_inline_data_with_xattr return -EINVAL."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50218",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50218\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-50218](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50218)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nocfs2: pass u64 to ocfs2_truncate_inline maybe overflow\n\nSyzbot reported a kernel BUG in ocfs2_truncate_inline.  There are two\nreasons for this: first, the parameter value passed is greater than\nocfs2_max_inline_data_with_xattr, second, the start and end parameters of\nocfs2_truncate_inline are \"unsigned int\".\n\nSo, we need to add a sanity check for byte_start and byte_len right before\nocfs2_truncate_inline() in ocfs2_remove_inode_range(), if they are greater\nthan ocfs2_max_inline_data_with_xattr return -EINVAL.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50218**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-50218](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50218)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nocfs2: pass u64 to ocfs2_truncate_inline maybe overflow\n\nSyzbot reported a kernel BUG in ocfs2_truncate_inline.  There are two\nreasons for this: first, the parameter value passed is greater than\nocfs2_max_inline_data_with_xattr, second, the start and end parameters of\nocfs2_truncate_inline are \"unsigned int\".\n\nSo, we need to add a sanity check for byte_start and byte_len right before\nocfs2_truncate_inline() in ocfs2_remove_inode_range(), if they are greater\nthan ocfs2_max_inline_data_with_xattr return -EINVAL."
              },
