            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50233",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: staging: iio: frequency: ad9832: fix division by zero in ad9832_calc_freqreg()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nstaging: iio: frequency: ad9832: fix division by zero in ad9832_calc_freqreg()\n\nIn the ad9832_write_frequency() function, clk_get_rate() might return 0.\nThis can lead to a division by zero when calling ad9832_calc_freqreg().\nThe check if (fout \u003e (clk_get_rate(st-\u003emclk) / 2)) does not protect\nagainst the case when fout is 0. The ad9832_write_frequency() function\nis called from ad9832_write(), and fout is derived from a text buffer,\nwhich can contain any value."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50233",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50233\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-56.58\nLink: [CVE-2024-50233](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50233)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nstaging: iio: frequency: ad9832: fix division by zero in ad9832_calc_freqreg()\n\nIn the ad9832_write_frequency() function, clk_get_rate() might return 0.\nThis can lead to a division by zero when calling ad9832_calc_freqreg().\nThe check if (fout \u003e (clk_get_rate(st-\u003emclk) / 2)) does not protect\nagainst the case when fout is 0. The ad9832_write_frequency() function\nis called from ad9832_write(), and fout is derived from a text buffer,\nwhich can contain any value.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50233**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-56.58|[CVE-2024-50233](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50233)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nstaging: iio: frequency: ad9832: fix division by zero in ad9832_calc_freqreg()\n\nIn the ad9832_write_frequency() function, clk_get_rate() might return 0.\nThis can lead to a division by zero when calling ad9832_calc_freqreg().\nThe check if (fout \u003e (clk_get_rate(st-\u003emclk) / 2)) does not protect\nagainst the case when fout is 0. The ad9832_write_frequency() function\nis called from ad9832_write(), and fout is derived from a text buffer,\nwhich can contain any value."
              },
