            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50259",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: netdevsim: Add trailing zero to terminate the string in nsim_nexthop_bucket_activity_write()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetdevsim: Add trailing zero to terminate the string in nsim_nexthop_bucket_activity_write()\n\nThis was found by a static analyzer.\nWe should not forget the trailing zero after copy_from_user()\nif we will further do some string operations, sscanf() in this\ncase. Adding a trailing zero will ensure that the function\nperforms properly."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50259",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50259\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-50259](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50259)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetdevsim: Add trailing zero to terminate the string in nsim_nexthop_bucket_activity_write()\n\nThis was found by a static analyzer.\nWe should not forget the trailing zero after copy_from_user()\nif we will further do some string operations, sscanf() in this\ncase. Adding a trailing zero will ensure that the function\nperforms properly.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50259**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-50259](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50259)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetdevsim: Add trailing zero to terminate the string in nsim_nexthop_bucket_activity_write()\n\nThis was found by a static analyzer.\nWe should not forget the trailing zero after copy_from_user()\nif we will further do some string operations, sscanf() in this\ncase. Adding a trailing zero will ensure that the function\nperforms properly."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
