            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50272",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: filemap: Fix bounds checking in filemap_read()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfilemap: Fix bounds checking in filemap_read()\n\nIf the caller supplies an iocb-\u003eki_pos value that is close to the\nfilesystem upper limit, and an iterator with a count that causes us to\noverflow that limit, then filemap_read() enters an infinite loop.\n\nThis behaviour was discovered when testing xfstests generic/525 with the\n\"localio\" optimisation for loopback NFS mounts."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50272",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50272\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-50272](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50272)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfilemap: Fix bounds checking in filemap_read()\n\nIf the caller supplies an iocb-\u003eki_pos value that is close to the\nfilesystem upper limit, and an iterator with a count that causes us to\noverflow that limit, then filemap_read() enters an infinite loop.\n\nThis behaviour was discovered when testing xfstests generic/525 with the\n\"localio\" optimisation for loopback NFS mounts.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50272**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-50272](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50272)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfilemap: Fix bounds checking in filemap_read()\n\nIf the caller supplies an iocb-\u003eki_pos value that is close to the\nfilesystem upper limit, and an iterator with a count that causes us to\noverflow that limit, then filemap_read() enters an infinite loop.\n\nThis behaviour was discovered when testing xfstests generic/525 with the\n\"localio\" optimisation for loopback NFS mounts."
              },
              "properties": {
