            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50284",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ksmbd: Fix the missing xa_store error check"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: Fix the missing xa_store error check\n\nxa_store() can fail, it return xa_err(-EINVAL) if the entry cannot\nbe stored in an XArray, or xa_err(-ENOMEM) if memory allocation failed,\nso check error for xa_store() to fix it."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50284",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50284\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-50284](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50284)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: Fix the missing xa_store error check\n\nxa_store() can fail, it return xa_err(-EINVAL) if the entry cannot\nbe stored in an XArray, or xa_err(-ENOMEM) if memory allocation failed,\nso check error for xa_store() to fix it.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50284**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-50284](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50284)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: Fix the missing xa_store error check\n\nxa_store() can fail, it return xa_err(-EINVAL) if the entry cannot\nbe stored in an XArray, or xa_err(-ENOMEM) if memory allocation failed,\nso check error for xa_store() to fix it."
