            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50287",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: media: v4l2-tpg: prevent the risk of a division by zero"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: v4l2-tpg: prevent the risk of a division by zero\n\nAs reported by Coverity, the logic at tpg_precalculate_line()\nblindly rescales the buffer even when scaled_witdh is equal to\nzero. If this ever happens, this will cause a division by zero.\n\nInstead, add a WARN_ON_ONCE() to trigger such cases and return\nwithout doing any precalculation."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50287",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50287\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-50287](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50287)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: v4l2-tpg: prevent the risk of a division by zero\n\nAs reported by Coverity, the logic at tpg_precalculate_line()\nblindly rescales the buffer even when scaled_witdh is equal to\nzero. If this ever happens, this will cause a division by zero.\n\nInstead, add a WARN_ON_ONCE() to trigger such cases and return\nwithout doing any precalculation.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50287**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-50287](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50287)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: v4l2-tpg: prevent the risk of a division by zero\n\nAs reported by Coverity, the logic at tpg_precalculate_line()\nblindly rescales the buffer even when scaled_witdh is equal to\nzero. If this ever happens, this will cause a division by zero.\n\nInstead, add a WARN_ON_ONCE() to trigger such cases and return\nwithout doing any precalculation."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50288",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: media: vivid: fix buffer overwrite when using \u003e 32 buffers"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: vivid: fix buffer overwrite when using \u003e 32 buffers\n\nThe maximum number of buffers that can be requested was increased to\n64 for the video capture queue. But video capture used a must_blank\narray that was still sized for 32 (VIDEO_MAX_FRAME). This caused an\nout-of-bounds write when using buffer indices \u003e= 32.\n\nCreate a new define MAX_VID_CAP_BUFFERS that is used to access the\nmust_blank array and set max_num_buffers for the video capture queue.\n\nThis solves a crash reported by:\n\n\thttps://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=219258"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50288",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50288\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-50288](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50288)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: vivid: fix buffer overwrite when using \u003e 32 buffers\n\nThe maximum number of buffers that can be requested was increased to\n64 for the video capture queue. But video capture used a must_blank\narray that was still sized for 32 (VIDEO_MAX_FRAME). This caused an\nout-of-bounds write when using buffer indices \u003e= 32.\n\nCreate a new define MAX_VID_CAP_BUFFERS that is used to access the\nmust_blank array and set max_num_buffers for the video capture queue.\n\nThis solves a crash reported by:\n\n\thttps://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=219258",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50288**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-50288](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50288)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: vivid: fix buffer overwrite when using \u003e 32 buffers\n\nThe maximum number of buffers that can be requested was increased to\n64 for the video capture queue. But video capture used a must_blank\narray that was still sized for 32 (VIDEO_MAX_FRAME). This caused an\nout-of-bounds write when using buffer indices \u003e= 32.\n\nCreate a new define MAX_VID_CAP_BUFFERS that is used to access the\nmust_blank array and set max_num_buffers for the video capture queue.\n\nThis solves a crash reported by:\n\n\thttps://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=219258"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
