            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50294",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: rxrpc: Fix missing locking causing hanging calls"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrxrpc: Fix missing locking causing hanging calls\n\nIf a call gets aborted (e.g. because kafs saw a signal) between it being\nqueued for connection and the I/O thread picking up the call, the abort\nwill be prioritised over the connection and it will be removed from\nlocal-\u003enew_client_calls by rxrpc_disconnect_client_call() without a lock\nbeing held.  This may cause other calls on the list to disappear if a race\noccurs.\n\nFix this by taking the client_call_lock when removing a call from whatever\nlist its -\u003ewait_link happens to be on."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50294",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50294\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-50294](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50294)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrxrpc: Fix missing locking causing hanging calls\n\nIf a call gets aborted (e.g. because kafs saw a signal) between it being\nqueued for connection and the I/O thread picking up the call, the abort\nwill be prioritised over the connection and it will be removed from\nlocal-\u003enew_client_calls by rxrpc_disconnect_client_call() without a lock\nbeing held.  This may cause other calls on the list to disappear if a race\noccurs.\n\nFix this by taking the client_call_lock when removing a call from whatever\nlist its -\u003ewait_link happens to be on.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50294**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-50294](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50294)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrxrpc: Fix missing locking causing hanging calls\n\nIf a call gets aborted (e.g. because kafs saw a signal) between it being\nqueued for connection and the I/O thread picking up the call, the abort\nwill be prioritised over the connection and it will be removed from\nlocal-\u003enew_client_calls by rxrpc_disconnect_client_call() without a lock\nbeing held.  This may cause other calls on the list to disappear if a race\noccurs.\n\nFix this by taking the client_call_lock when removing a call from whatever\nlist its -\u003ewait_link happens to be on."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-50295",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: net: arc: fix the device for dma_map_single/dma_unmap_single"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: arc: fix the device for dma_map_single/dma_unmap_single\n\nThe ndev-\u003edev and pdev-\u003edev aren't the same device, use ndev-\u003edev.parent\nwhich has dma_mask, ndev-\u003edev.parent is just pdev-\u003edev.\nOr it would cause the following issue:\n\n[   39.933526] ------------[ cut here ]------------\n[   39.938414] WARNING: CPU: 1 PID: 501 at kernel/dma/mapping.c:149 dma_map_page_attrs+0x90/0x1f8"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50295",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-50295\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-50295](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50295)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: arc: fix the device for dma_map_single/dma_unmap_single\n\nThe ndev-\u003edev and pdev-\u003edev aren't the same device, use ndev-\u003edev.parent\nwhich has dma_mask, ndev-\u003edev.parent is just pdev-\u003edev.\nOr it would cause the following issue:\n\n[   39.933526] ------------[ cut here ]------------\n[   39.938414] WARNING: CPU: 1 PID: 501 at kernel/dma/mapping.c:149 dma_map_page_attrs+0x90/0x1f8",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-50295**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-50295](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-50295)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: arc: fix the device for dma_map_single/dma_unmap_single\n\nThe ndev-\u003edev and pdev-\u003edev aren't the same device, use ndev-\u003edev.parent\nwhich has dma_mask, ndev-\u003edev.parent is just pdev-\u003edev.\nOr it would cause the following issue:\n\n[   39.933526] ------------[ cut here ]------------\n[   39.938414] WARNING: CPU: 1 PID: 501 at kernel/dma/mapping.c:149 dma_map_page_attrs+0x90/0x1f8"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
