            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-52332",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: igb: Fix potential invalid memory access in igb_init_module()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nigb: Fix potential invalid memory access in igb_init_module()\n\nThe pci_register_driver() can fail and when this happened, the dca_notifier\nneeds to be unregistered, otherwise the dca_notifier can be called when\nigb fails to install, resulting to invalid memory access."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-52332",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-52332\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-52332](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-52332)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nigb: Fix potential invalid memory access in igb_init_module()\n\nThe pci_register_driver() can fail and when this happened, the dca_notifier\nneeds to be unregistered, otherwise the dca_notifier can be called when\nigb fails to install, resulting to invalid memory access.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-52332**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-52332](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-52332)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nigb: Fix potential invalid memory access in igb_init_module()\n\nThe pci_register_driver() can fail and when this happened, the dca_notifier\nneeds to be unregistered, otherwise the dca_notifier can be called when\nigb fails to install, resulting to invalid memory access."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-52559",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/msm/gem: prevent integer overflow in msm_ioctl_gem_submit()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/msm/gem: prevent integer overflow in msm_ioctl_gem_submit()\n\nThe \"submit-\u003ecmd[i].size\" and \"submit-\u003ecmd[i].offset\" variables are u32\nvalues that come from the user via the submit_lookup_cmds() function.\nThis addition could lead to an integer wrapping bug so use size_add()\nto prevent that.\n\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/624696/"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-52559",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-52559\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-78.78\nLink: [CVE-2024-52559](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-52559)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/msm/gem: prevent integer overflow in msm_ioctl_gem_submit()\n\nThe \"submit-\u003ecmd[i].size\" and \"submit-\u003ecmd[i].offset\" variables are u32\nvalues that come from the user via the submit_lookup_cmds() function.\nThis addition could lead to an integer wrapping bug so use size_add()\nto prevent that.\n\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/624696/",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-52559**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-78.78|[CVE-2024-52559](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-52559)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/msm/gem: prevent integer overflow in msm_ioctl_gem_submit()\n\nThe \"submit-\u003ecmd[i].size\" and \"submit-\u003ecmd[i].offset\" variables are u32\nvalues that come from the user via the submit_lookup_cmds() function.\nThis addition could lead to an integer wrapping bug so use size_add()\nto prevent that.\n\nPatchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/624696/"
              },
              "properties": {
