            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-53043",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: mctp i2c: handle NULL header address"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmctp i2c: handle NULL header address\n\ndaddr can be NULL if there is no neighbour table entry present,\nin that case the tx packet should be dropped.\n\nsaddr will usually be set by MCTP core, but check for NULL in case a\npacket is transmitted by a different protocol."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53043",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53043\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-53043](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53043)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmctp i2c: handle NULL header address\n\ndaddr can be NULL if there is no neighbour table entry present,\nin that case the tx packet should be dropped.\n\nsaddr will usually be set by MCTP core, but check for NULL in case a\npacket is transmitted by a different protocol.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-53043**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-53043](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53043)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmctp i2c: handle NULL header address\n\ndaddr can be NULL if there is no neighbour table entry present,\nin that case the tx packet should be dropped.\n\nsaddr will usually be set by MCTP core, but check for NULL in case a\npacket is transmitted by a different protocol."
