            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-53051",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/i915/hdcp: Add encoder check in intel_hdcp_get_capability"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/i915/hdcp: Add encoder check in intel_hdcp_get_capability\n\nSometimes during hotplug scenario or suspend/resume scenario encoder is\nnot always initialized when intel_hdcp_get_capability add\na check to avoid kernel null pointer dereference."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53051",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53051\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-53051](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53051)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/i915/hdcp: Add encoder check in intel_hdcp_get_capability\n\nSometimes during hotplug scenario or suspend/resume scenario encoder is\nnot always initialized when intel_hdcp_get_capability add\na check to avoid kernel null pointer dereference.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-53051**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-53051](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53051)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/i915/hdcp: Add encoder check in intel_hdcp_get_capability\n\nSometimes during hotplug scenario or suspend/resume scenario encoder is\nnot always initialized when intel_hdcp_get_capability add\na check to avoid kernel null pointer dereference."
