            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-53062",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: media: mgb4: protect driver against spectre"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: mgb4: protect driver against spectre\n\nFrequency range is set from sysfs via frequency_range_store(),\nbeing vulnerable to spectre, as reported by smatch:\n\n\tdrivers/media/pci/mgb4/mgb4_cmt.c:231 mgb4_cmt_set_vin_freq_range() warn: potential spectre issue 'cmt_vals_in' [r]\n\tdrivers/media/pci/mgb4/mgb4_cmt.c:238 mgb4_cmt_set_vin_freq_range() warn: possible spectre second half.  'reg_set'\n\nFix it."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53062",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53062\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-53062](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53062)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: mgb4: protect driver against spectre\n\nFrequency range is set from sysfs via frequency_range_store(),\nbeing vulnerable to spectre, as reported by smatch:\n\n\tdrivers/media/pci/mgb4/mgb4_cmt.c:231 mgb4_cmt_set_vin_freq_range() warn: potential spectre issue 'cmt_vals_in' [r]\n\tdrivers/media/pci/mgb4/mgb4_cmt.c:238 mgb4_cmt_set_vin_freq_range() warn: possible spectre second half.  'reg_set'\n\nFix it.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-53062**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-53062](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53062)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: mgb4: protect driver against spectre\n\nFrequency range is set from sysfs via frequency_range_store(),\nbeing vulnerable to spectre, as reported by smatch:\n\n\tdrivers/media/pci/mgb4/mgb4_cmt.c:231 mgb4_cmt_set_vin_freq_range() warn: potential spectre issue 'cmt_vals_in' [r]\n\tdrivers/media/pci/mgb4/mgb4_cmt.c:238 mgb4_cmt_set_vin_freq_range() warn: possible spectre second half.  'reg_set'\n\nFix it."
