            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-53083",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: usb: typec: qcom-pmic: init value of hdr_len/txbuf_len earlier"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: typec: qcom-pmic: init value of hdr_len/txbuf_len earlier\n\nIf the read of USB_PDPHY_RX_ACKNOWLEDGE_REG failed, then hdr_len and\ntxbuf_len are uninitialized. This commit stops to print uninitialized\nvalue and misleading/false data."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53083",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53083\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-53083](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53083)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: typec: qcom-pmic: init value of hdr_len/txbuf_len earlier\n\nIf the read of USB_PDPHY_RX_ACKNOWLEDGE_REG failed, then hdr_len and\ntxbuf_len are uninitialized. This commit stops to print uninitialized\nvalue and misleading/false data.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-53083**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-53083](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53083)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: typec: qcom-pmic: init value of hdr_len/txbuf_len earlier\n\nIf the read of USB_PDPHY_RX_ACKNOWLEDGE_REG failed, then hdr_len and\ntxbuf_len are uninitialized. This commit stops to print uninitialized\nvalue and misleading/false data."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
