            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-53099",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: bpf: Check validity of link-\u003etype in bpf_link_show_fdinfo()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Check validity of link-\u003etype in bpf_link_show_fdinfo()\n\nIf a newly-added link type doesn't invoke BPF_LINK_TYPE(), accessing\nbpf_link_type_strs[link-\u003etype] may result in an out-of-bounds access.\n\nTo spot such missed invocations early in the future, checking the\nvalidity of link-\u003etype in bpf_link_show_fdinfo() and emitting a warning\nwhen such invocations are missed."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53099",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53099\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-53099](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53099)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Check validity of link-\u003etype in bpf_link_show_fdinfo()\n\nIf a newly-added link type doesn't invoke BPF_LINK_TYPE(), accessing\nbpf_link_type_strs[link-\u003etype] may result in an out-of-bounds access.\n\nTo spot such missed invocations early in the future, checking the\nvalidity of link-\u003etype in bpf_link_show_fdinfo() and emitting a warning\nwhen such invocations are missed.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-53099**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-53099](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53099)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Check validity of link-\u003etype in bpf_link_show_fdinfo()\n\nIf a newly-added link type doesn't invoke BPF_LINK_TYPE(), accessing\nbpf_link_type_strs[link-\u003etype] may result in an out-of-bounds access.\n\nTo spot such missed invocations early in the future, checking the\nvalidity of link-\u003etype in bpf_link_show_fdinfo() and emitting a warning\nwhen such invocations are missed."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
