            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-53106",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ima: fix buffer overrun in ima_eventdigest_init_common"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nima: fix buffer overrun in ima_eventdigest_init_common\n\nFunction ima_eventdigest_init() calls ima_eventdigest_init_common()\nwith HASH_ALGO__LAST which is then used to access the array\nhash_digest_size[] leading to buffer overrun. Have a conditional\nstatement to handle this."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53106",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53106\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-53106](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53106)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nima: fix buffer overrun in ima_eventdigest_init_common\n\nFunction ima_eventdigest_init() calls ima_eventdigest_init_common()\nwith HASH_ALGO__LAST which is then used to access the array\nhash_digest_size[] leading to buffer overrun. Have a conditional\nstatement to handle this.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-53106**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-53106](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53106)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nima: fix buffer overrun in ima_eventdigest_init_common\n\nFunction ima_eventdigest_init() calls ima_eventdigest_init_common()\nwith HASH_ALGO__LAST which is then used to access the array\nhash_digest_size[] leading to buffer overrun. Have a conditional\nstatement to handle this."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
