            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-53107",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: fs/proc/task_mmu: prevent integer overflow in pagemap_scan_get_args()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfs/proc/task_mmu: prevent integer overflow in pagemap_scan_get_args()\n\nThe \"arg-\u003evec_len\" variable is a u64 that comes from the user at the start\nof the function.  The \"arg-\u003evec_len * sizeof(struct page_region))\"\nmultiplication can lead to integer wrapping.  Use size_mul() to avoid\nthat.\n\nAlso the size_add/mul() functions work on unsigned long so for 32bit\nsystems we need to ensure that \"arg-\u003evec_len\" fits in an unsigned long."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53107",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53107\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-53107](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53107)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfs/proc/task_mmu: prevent integer overflow in pagemap_scan_get_args()\n\nThe \"arg-\u003evec_len\" variable is a u64 that comes from the user at the start\nof the function.  The \"arg-\u003evec_len * sizeof(struct page_region))\"\nmultiplication can lead to integer wrapping.  Use size_mul() to avoid\nthat.\n\nAlso the size_add/mul() functions work on unsigned long so for 32bit\nsystems we need to ensure that \"arg-\u003evec_len\" fits in an unsigned long.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-53107**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-53107](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53107)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfs/proc/task_mmu: prevent integer overflow in pagemap_scan_get_args()\n\nThe \"arg-\u003evec_len\" variable is a u64 that comes from the user at the start\nof the function.  The \"arg-\u003evec_len * sizeof(struct page_region))\"\nmultiplication can lead to integer wrapping.  Use size_mul() to avoid\nthat.\n\nAlso the size_add/mul() functions work on unsigned long so for 32bit\nsystems we need to ensure that \"arg-\u003evec_len\" fits in an unsigned long."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-53108",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/amd/display: Adjust VSDB parser for replay feature"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Adjust VSDB parser for replay feature\n\nAt some point, the IEEE ID identification for the replay check in the\nAMD EDID was added. However, this check causes the following\nout-of-bounds issues when using KASAN:\n\n[   27.804016] BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps+0xefa/0x17a0 [amdgpu]\n[   27.804788] Read of size 1 at addr ffff8881647fdb00 by task systemd-udevd/383\n\n...\n\n[   27.821207] Memory state around the buggy address:\n[   27.821215]  ffff8881647fda00: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00\n[   27.821224]  ffff8881647fda80: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00\n[   27.821234] \u003effff8881647fdb00: fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc\n[   27.821243]                    ^\n[   27.821250]  ffff8881647fdb80: fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc\n[   27.821259]  ffff8881647fdc00: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00\n[   27.821268] ==================================================================\n\nThis is caused because the ID extraction happens outside of the range of\nthe edid lenght. This commit addresses this issue by considering the\namd_vsdb_block size.\n\n(cherry picked from commit b7e381b1ccd5e778e3d9c44c669ad38439a861d8)"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53108",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53108\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-53108](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53108)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Adjust VSDB parser for replay feature\n\nAt some point, the IEEE ID identification for the replay check in the\nAMD EDID was added. However, this check causes the following\nout-of-bounds issues when using KASAN:\n\n[   27.804016] BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps+0xefa/0x17a0 [amdgpu]\n[   27.804788] Read of size 1 at addr ffff8881647fdb00 by task systemd-udevd/383\n\n...\n\n[   27.821207] Memory state around the buggy address:\n[   27.821215]  ffff8881647fda00: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00\n[   27.821224]  ffff8881647fda80: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00\n[   27.821234] \u003effff8881647fdb00: fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc\n[   27.821243]                    ^\n[   27.821250]  ffff8881647fdb80: fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc\n[   27.821259]  ffff8881647fdc00: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00\n[   27.821268] ==================================================================\n\nThis is caused because the ID extraction happens outside of the range of\nthe edid lenght. This commit addresses this issue by considering the\namd_vsdb_block size.\n\n(cherry picked from commit b7e381b1ccd5e778e3d9c44c669ad38439a861d8)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-53108**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-53108](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53108)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/display: Adjust VSDB parser for replay feature\n\nAt some point, the IEEE ID identification for the replay check in the\nAMD EDID was added. However, this check causes the following\nout-of-bounds issues when using KASAN:\n\n[   27.804016] BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps+0xefa/0x17a0 [amdgpu]\n[   27.804788] Read of size 1 at addr ffff8881647fdb00 by task systemd-udevd/383\n\n...\n\n[   27.821207] Memory state around the buggy address:\n[   27.821215]  ffff8881647fda00: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00\n[   27.821224]  ffff8881647fda80: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00\n[   27.821234] \u003effff8881647fdb00: fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc\n[   27.821243]                    ^\n[   27.821250]  ffff8881647fdb80: fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc fc\n[   27.821259]  ffff8881647fdc00: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00\n[   27.821268] ==================================================================\n\nThis is caused because the ID extraction happens outside of the range of\nthe edid lenght. This commit addresses this issue by considering the\namd_vsdb_block size.\n\n(cherry picked from commit b7e381b1ccd5e778e3d9c44c669ad38439a861d8)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-53109",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: nommu: pass NULL argument to vma_iter_prealloc()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnommu: pass NULL argument to vma_iter_prealloc()\n\nWhen deleting a vma entry from a maple tree, it has to pass NULL to\nvma_iter_prealloc() in order to calculate internal state of the tree, but\nit passed a wrong argument.  As a result, nommu kernels crashed upon\naccessing a vma iterator, such as acct_collect() reading the size of vma\nentries after do_munmap().\n\nThis commit fixes this issue by passing a right argument to the\npreallocation call."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53109",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53109\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-53109](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53109)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnommu: pass NULL argument to vma_iter_prealloc()\n\nWhen deleting a vma entry from a maple tree, it has to pass NULL to\nvma_iter_prealloc() in order to calculate internal state of the tree, but\nit passed a wrong argument.  As a result, nommu kernels crashed upon\naccessing a vma iterator, such as acct_collect() reading the size of vma\nentries after do_munmap().\n\nThis commit fixes this issue by passing a right argument to the\npreallocation call.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-53109**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-53109](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53109)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnommu: pass NULL argument to vma_iter_prealloc()\n\nWhen deleting a vma entry from a maple tree, it has to pass NULL to\nvma_iter_prealloc() in order to calculate internal state of the tree, but\nit passed a wrong argument.  As a result, nommu kernels crashed upon\naccessing a vma iterator, such as acct_collect() reading the size of vma\nentries after do_munmap().\n\nThis commit fixes this issue by passing a right argument to the\npreallocation call."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
