            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-53114",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: x86/CPU/AMD: Clear virtualized VMLOAD/VMSAVE on Zen4 client"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nx86/CPU/AMD: Clear virtualized VMLOAD/VMSAVE on Zen4 client\n\nA number of Zen4 client SoCs advertise the ability to use virtualized\nVMLOAD/VMSAVE, but using these instructions is reported to be a cause\nof a random host reboot.\n\nThese instructions aren't intended to be advertised on Zen4 client\nso clear the capability."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53114",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53114\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-53114](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53114)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nx86/CPU/AMD: Clear virtualized VMLOAD/VMSAVE on Zen4 client\n\nA number of Zen4 client SoCs advertise the ability to use virtualized\nVMLOAD/VMSAVE, but using these instructions is reported to be a cause\nof a random host reboot.\n\nThese instructions aren't intended to be advertised on Zen4 client\nso clear the capability.",
