            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-53122",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: mptcp: cope racing subflow creation in mptcp_rcv_space_adjust"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmptcp: cope racing subflow creation in mptcp_rcv_space_adjust\n\nAdditional active subflows - i.e. created by the in kernel path\nmanager - are included into the subflow list before starting the\n3whs.\n\nA racing recvmsg() spooling data received on an already established\nsubflow would unconditionally call tcp_cleanup_rbuf() on all the\ncurrent subflows, potentially hitting a divide by zero error on\nthe newly created ones.\n\nExplicitly check that the subflow is in a suitable state before\ninvoking tcp_cleanup_rbuf()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53122",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53122\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-53122](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53122)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmptcp: cope racing subflow creation in mptcp_rcv_space_adjust\n\nAdditional active subflows - i.e. created by the in kernel path\nmanager - are included into the subflow list before starting the\n3whs.\n\nA racing recvmsg() spooling data received on an already established\nsubflow would unconditionally call tcp_cleanup_rbuf() on all the\ncurrent subflows, potentially hitting a divide by zero error on\nthe newly created ones.\n\nExplicitly check that the subflow is in a suitable state before\ninvoking tcp_cleanup_rbuf().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-53122**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-53122](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53122)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmptcp: cope racing subflow creation in mptcp_rcv_space_adjust\n\nAdditional active subflows - i.e. created by the in kernel path\nmanager - are included into the subflow list before starting the\n3whs.\n\nA racing recvmsg() spooling data received on an already established\nsubflow would unconditionally call tcp_cleanup_rbuf() on all the\ncurrent subflows, potentially hitting a divide by zero error on\nthe newly created ones.\n\nExplicitly check that the subflow is in a suitable state before\ninvoking tcp_cleanup_rbuf()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
