              "id": "CVE-2024-53146",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: NFSD: Prevent a potential integer overflow"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nNFSD: Prevent a potential integer overflow\n\nIf the tag length is \u003e= U32_MAX - 3 then the \"length + 4\" addition\ncan result in an integer overflow. Address this by splitting the\ndecoding into several steps so that decode_cb_compound4res() does\nnot have to perform arithmetic on the unsafe length value."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53146",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53146\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-53146](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53146)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nNFSD: Prevent a potential integer overflow\n\nIf the tag length is \u003e= U32_MAX - 3 then the \"length + 4\" addition\ncan result in an integer overflow. Address this by splitting the\ndecoding into several steps so that decode_cb_compound4res() does\nnot have to perform arithmetic on the unsafe length value.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-53146**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-53146](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53146)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nNFSD: Prevent a potential integer overflow\n\nIf the tag length is \u003e= U32_MAX - 3 then the \"length + 4\" addition\ncan result in an integer overflow. Address this by splitting the\ndecoding into several steps so that decode_cb_compound4res() does\nnot have to perform arithmetic on the unsafe length value."
              },
