              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: crypto: qat/qat_4xxx - fix off by one in uof_get_name()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: qat/qat_4xxx - fix off by one in uof_get_name()\n\nThe fw_objs[] array has \"num_objs\" elements so the \u003e needs to be \u003e= to\nprevent an out of bounds read."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53162",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53162\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-53162](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53162)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: qat/qat_4xxx - fix off by one in uof_get_name()\n\nThe fw_objs[] array has \"num_objs\" elements so the \u003e needs to be \u003e= to\nprevent an out of bounds read.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-53162**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-53162](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53162)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: qat/qat_4xxx - fix off by one in uof_get_name()\n\nThe fw_objs[] array has \"num_objs\" elements so the \u003e needs to be \u003e= to\nprevent an out of bounds read."
              },
