            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-53202",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: firmware_loader: Fix possible resource leak in fw_log_firmware_info()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfirmware_loader: Fix possible resource leak in fw_log_firmware_info()\n\nThe alg instance should be released under the exception path, otherwise\nthere may be resource leak here.\n\nTo mitigate this, free the alg instance with crypto_free_shash when kmalloc\nfails."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53202",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53202\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-53202](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53202)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfirmware_loader: Fix possible resource leak in fw_log_firmware_info()\n\nThe alg instance should be released under the exception path, otherwise\nthere may be resource leak here.\n\nTo mitigate this, free the alg instance with crypto_free_shash when kmalloc\nfails.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-53202**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-53202](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53202)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfirmware_loader: Fix possible resource leak in fw_log_firmware_info()\n\nThe alg instance should be released under the exception path, otherwise\nthere may be resource leak here.\n\nTo mitigate this, free the alg instance with crypto_free_shash when kmalloc\nfails."
              },
