              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53231",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-53231\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-53231](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53231)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncpufreq: CPPC: Fix possible null-ptr-deref for cpufreq_cpu_get_raw()\n\ncpufreq_cpu_get_raw() may return NULL if the cpu is not in\npolicy-\u003ecpus cpu mask and it will cause null pointer dereference.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-53231**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-53231](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-53231)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncpufreq: CPPC: Fix possible null-ptr-deref for cpufreq_cpu_get_raw()\n\ncpufreq_cpu_get_raw() may return NULL if the cpu is not in\npolicy-\u003ecpus cpu mask and it will cause null pointer dereference."
