            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56369",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/modes: Avoid divide by zero harder in drm_mode_vrefresh()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/modes: Avoid divide by zero harder in drm_mode_vrefresh()\n\ndrm_mode_vrefresh() is trying to avoid divide by zero\nby checking whether htotal or vtotal are zero. But we may\nstill end up with a div-by-zero of vtotal*htotal*..."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56369",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56369\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-60.63\nLink: [CVE-2024-56369](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56369)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/modes: Avoid divide by zero harder in drm_mode_vrefresh()\n\ndrm_mode_vrefresh() is trying to avoid divide by zero\nby checking whether htotal or vtotal are zero. But we may\nstill end up with a div-by-zero of vtotal*htotal*...",
