            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56561",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: PCI: endpoint: Fix PCI domain ID release in pci_epc_destroy()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: endpoint: Fix PCI domain ID release in pci_epc_destroy()\n\npci_epc_destroy() invokes pci_bus_release_domain_nr() to release the PCI\ndomain ID, but there are two issues:\n\n  - 'epc-\u003edev' is passed to pci_bus_release_domain_nr() which was already\n    freed by device_unregister(), leading to a use-after-free issue.\n\n  - Domain ID corresponds to the EPC device parent, so passing 'epc-\u003edev'\n    is also wrong.\n\nFix these issues by passing 'epc-\u003edev.parent' to\npci_bus_release_domain_nr() and also do it before device_unregister().\n\n[mani: reworded subject and description]"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56561",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56561\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56561](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56561)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: endpoint: Fix PCI domain ID release in pci_epc_destroy()\n\npci_epc_destroy() invokes pci_bus_release_domain_nr() to release the PCI\ndomain ID, but there are two issues:\n\n  - 'epc-\u003edev' is passed to pci_bus_release_domain_nr() which was already\n    freed by device_unregister(), leading to a use-after-free issue.\n\n  - Domain ID corresponds to the EPC device parent, so passing 'epc-\u003edev'\n    is also wrong.\n\nFix these issues by passing 'epc-\u003edev.parent' to\npci_bus_release_domain_nr() and also do it before device_unregister().\n\n[mani: reworded subject and description]",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56561**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56561](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56561)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: endpoint: Fix PCI domain ID release in pci_epc_destroy()\n\npci_epc_destroy() invokes pci_bus_release_domain_nr() to release the PCI\ndomain ID, but there are two issues:\n\n  - 'epc-\u003edev' is passed to pci_bus_release_domain_nr() which was already\n    freed by device_unregister(), leading to a use-after-free issue.\n\n  - Domain ID corresponds to the EPC device parent, so passing 'epc-\u003edev'\n    is also wrong.\n\nFix these issues by passing 'epc-\u003edev.parent' to\npci_bus_release_domain_nr() and also do it before device_unregister().\n\n[mani: reworded subject and description]"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
