            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56570",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ovl: Filter invalid inodes with missing lookup function"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\novl: Filter invalid inodes with missing lookup function\n\nAdd a check to the ovl_dentry_weird() function to prevent the\nprocessing of directory inodes that lack the lookup function.\nThis is important because such inodes can cause errors in overlayfs\nwhen passed to the lowerstack."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56570",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56570\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56570](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56570)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\novl: Filter invalid inodes with missing lookup function\n\nAdd a check to the ovl_dentry_weird() function to prevent the\nprocessing of directory inodes that lack the lookup function.\nThis is important because such inodes can cause errors in overlayfs\nwhen passed to the lowerstack.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56570**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56570](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56570)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\novl: Filter invalid inodes with missing lookup function\n\nAdd a check to the ovl_dentry_weird() function to prevent the\nprocessing of directory inodes that lack the lookup function.\nThis is important because such inodes can cause errors in overlayfs\nwhen passed to the lowerstack."
              },
