            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56590",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: Bluetooth: hci_core: Fix not checking skb length on hci_acldata_packet"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: hci_core: Fix not checking skb length on hci_acldata_packet\n\nThis fixes not checking if skb really contains an ACL header otherwise\nthe code may attempt to access some uninitilized/invalid memory past the\nvalid skb-\u003edata."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56590",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56590\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56590](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56590)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: hci_core: Fix not checking skb length on hci_acldata_packet\n\nThis fixes not checking if skb really contains an ACL header otherwise\nthe code may attempt to access some uninitilized/invalid memory past the\nvalid skb-\u003edata.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56590**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56590](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56590)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: hci_core: Fix not checking skb length on hci_acldata_packet\n\nThis fixes not checking if skb really contains an ACL header otherwise\nthe code may attempt to access some uninitilized/invalid memory past the\nvalid skb-\u003edata."
              },
