            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56597",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: jfs: fix shift-out-of-bounds in dbSplit"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\njfs: fix shift-out-of-bounds in dbSplit\n\nWhen dmt_budmin is less than zero, it causes errors\nin the later stages. Added a check to return an error beforehand\nin dbAllocCtl itself."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56597",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56597\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56597](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56597)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\njfs: fix shift-out-of-bounds in dbSplit\n\nWhen dmt_budmin is less than zero, it causes errors\nin the later stages. Added a check to return an error beforehand\nin dbAllocCtl itself.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56597**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56597](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56597)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\njfs: fix shift-out-of-bounds in dbSplit\n\nWhen dmt_budmin is less than zero, it causes errors\nin the later stages. Added a check to return an error beforehand\nin dbAllocCtl itself."
              },
