            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56626",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ksmbd: fix Out-of-Bounds Write in ksmbd_vfs_stream_write"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix Out-of-Bounds Write in ksmbd_vfs_stream_write\n\nAn offset from client could be a negative value, It could allows\nto write data outside the bounds of the allocated buffer.\nNote that this issue is coming when setting\n'vfs objects = streams_xattr parameter' in ksmbd.conf."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56626",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56626\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56626](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56626)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix Out-of-Bounds Write in ksmbd_vfs_stream_write\n\nAn offset from client could be a negative value, It could allows\nto write data outside the bounds of the allocated buffer.\nNote that this issue is coming when setting\n'vfs objects = streams_xattr parameter' in ksmbd.conf.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56626**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56626](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56626)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix Out-of-Bounds Write in ksmbd_vfs_stream_write\n\nAn offset from client could be a negative value, It could allows\nto write data outside the bounds of the allocated buffer.\nNote that this issue is coming when setting\n'vfs objects = streams_xattr parameter' in ksmbd.conf."
