              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56632",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56632\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56632](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56632)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvme-tcp: fix the memleak while create new ctrl failed\n\nNow while we create new ctrl failed, we have not free the\ntagset occupied by admin_q, here try to fix it.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56632**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56632](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56632)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvme-tcp: fix the memleak while create new ctrl failed\n\nNow while we create new ctrl failed, we have not free the\ntagset occupied by admin_q, here try to fix it."
              },
