            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56634",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: gpio: grgpio: Add NULL check in grgpio_probe"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngpio: grgpio: Add NULL check in grgpio_probe\n\ndevm_kasprintf() can return a NULL pointer on failure,but this\nreturned value in grgpio_probe is not checked.\nAdd NULL check in grgpio_probe, to handle kernel NULL\npointer dereference error."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56634",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56634\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56634](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56634)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngpio: grgpio: Add NULL check in grgpio_probe\n\ndevm_kasprintf() can return a NULL pointer on failure,but this\nreturned value in grgpio_probe is not checked.\nAdd NULL check in grgpio_probe, to handle kernel NULL\npointer dereference error.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56634**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56634](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56634)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngpio: grgpio: Add NULL check in grgpio_probe\n\ndevm_kasprintf() can return a NULL pointer on failure,but this\nreturned value in grgpio_probe is not checked.\nAdd NULL check in grgpio_probe, to handle kernel NULL\npointer dereference error."
              },
