            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56689",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: PCI: endpoint: epf-mhi: Avoid NULL dereference if DT lacks 'mmio'"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: endpoint: epf-mhi: Avoid NULL dereference if DT lacks 'mmio'\n\nIf platform_get_resource_byname() fails and returns NULL because DT lacks\nan 'mmio' property for the MHI endpoint, dereferencing res-\u003estart will\ncause a NULL pointer access. Add a check to prevent it.\n\n[kwilczynski: error message update per the review feedback]\n[bhelgaas: commit log]"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56689",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56689\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56689](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56689)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: endpoint: epf-mhi: Avoid NULL dereference if DT lacks 'mmio'\n\nIf platform_get_resource_byname() fails and returns NULL because DT lacks\nan 'mmio' property for the MHI endpoint, dereferencing res-\u003estart will\ncause a NULL pointer access. Add a check to prevent it.\n\n[kwilczynski: error message update per the review feedback]\n[bhelgaas: commit log]",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56689**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56689](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56689)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: endpoint: epf-mhi: Avoid NULL dereference if DT lacks 'mmio'\n\nIf platform_get_resource_byname() fails and returns NULL because DT lacks\nan 'mmio' property for the MHI endpoint, dereferencing res-\u003estart will\ncause a NULL pointer access. Add a check to prevent it.\n\n[kwilczynski: error message update per the review feedback]\n[bhelgaas: commit log]"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56690",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: crypto: pcrypt - Call crypto layer directly when padata_do_parallel() return -EBUSY"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: pcrypt - Call crypto layer directly when padata_do_parallel() return -EBUSY\n\nSince commit 8f4f68e788c3 (\"crypto: pcrypt - Fix hungtask for\nPADATA_RESET\"), the pcrypt encryption and decryption operations return\n-EAGAIN when the CPU goes online or offline. In alg_test(), a WARN is\ngenerated when pcrypt_aead_decrypt() or pcrypt_aead_encrypt() returns\n-EAGAIN, the unnecessary panic will occur when panic_on_warn set 1.\nFix this issue by calling crypto layer directly without parallelization\nin that case."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56690",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56690\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56690](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56690)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: pcrypt - Call crypto layer directly when padata_do_parallel() return -EBUSY\n\nSince commit 8f4f68e788c3 (\"crypto: pcrypt - Fix hungtask for\nPADATA_RESET\"), the pcrypt encryption and decryption operations return\n-EAGAIN when the CPU goes online or offline. In alg_test(), a WARN is\ngenerated when pcrypt_aead_decrypt() or pcrypt_aead_encrypt() returns\n-EAGAIN, the unnecessary panic will occur when panic_on_warn set 1.\nFix this issue by calling crypto layer directly without parallelization\nin that case.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56690**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56690](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56690)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: pcrypt - Call crypto layer directly when padata_do_parallel() return -EBUSY\n\nSince commit 8f4f68e788c3 (\"crypto: pcrypt - Fix hungtask for\nPADATA_RESET\"), the pcrypt encryption and decryption operations return\n-EAGAIN when the CPU goes online or offline. In alg_test(), a WARN is\ngenerated when pcrypt_aead_decrypt() or pcrypt_aead_encrypt() returns\n-EAGAIN, the unnecessary panic will occur when panic_on_warn set 1.\nFix this issue by calling crypto layer directly without parallelization\nin that case."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56691",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: mfd: intel_soc_pmic_bxtwc: Use IRQ domain for USB Type-C device"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmfd: intel_soc_pmic_bxtwc: Use IRQ domain for USB Type-C device\n\nWhile design wise the idea of converting the driver to use\nthe hierarchy of the IRQ chips is correct, the implementation\nhas (inherited) flaws. This was unveiled when platform_get_irq()\nhad started WARN() on IRQ 0 that is supposed to be a Linux\nIRQ number (also known as vIRQ).\n\nRework the driver to respect IRQ domain when creating each MFD\ndevice separately, as the domain is not the same for all of them."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56691",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56691\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56691](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56691)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmfd: intel_soc_pmic_bxtwc: Use IRQ domain for USB Type-C device\n\nWhile design wise the idea of converting the driver to use\nthe hierarchy of the IRQ chips is correct, the implementation\nhas (inherited) flaws. This was unveiled when platform_get_irq()\nhad started WARN() on IRQ 0 that is supposed to be a Linux\nIRQ number (also known as vIRQ).\n\nRework the driver to respect IRQ domain when creating each MFD\ndevice separately, as the domain is not the same for all of them.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56691**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56691](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56691)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmfd: intel_soc_pmic_bxtwc: Use IRQ domain for USB Type-C device\n\nWhile design wise the idea of converting the driver to use\nthe hierarchy of the IRQ chips is correct, the implementation\nhas (inherited) flaws. This was unveiled when platform_get_irq()\nhad started WARN() on IRQ 0 that is supposed to be a Linux\nIRQ number (also known as vIRQ).\n\nRework the driver to respect IRQ domain when creating each MFD\ndevice separately, as the domain is not the same for all of them."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
