            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56720",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: bpf, sockmap: Several fixes to bpf_msg_pop_data"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf, sockmap: Several fixes to bpf_msg_pop_data\n\nSeveral fixes to bpf_msg_pop_data,\n1. In sk_msg_shift_left, we should put_page\n2. if (len == 0), return early is better\n3. pop the entire sk_msg (last == msg-\u003esg.size) should be supported\n4. Fix for the value of variable \"a\"\n5. In sk_msg_shift_left, after shifting, i has already pointed to the next\nelement. Addtional sk_msg_iter_var_next may result in BUG."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56720",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56720\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56720](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56720)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf, sockmap: Several fixes to bpf_msg_pop_data\n\nSeveral fixes to bpf_msg_pop_data,\n1. In sk_msg_shift_left, we should put_page\n2. if (len == 0), return early is better\n3. pop the entire sk_msg (last == msg-\u003esg.size) should be supported\n4. Fix for the value of variable \"a\"\n5. In sk_msg_shift_left, after shifting, i has already pointed to the next\nelement. Addtional sk_msg_iter_var_next may result in BUG.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56720**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56720](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56720)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf, sockmap: Several fixes to bpf_msg_pop_data\n\nSeveral fixes to bpf_msg_pop_data,\n1. In sk_msg_shift_left, we should put_page\n2. if (len == 0), return early is better\n3. pop the entire sk_msg (last == msg-\u003esg.size) should be supported\n4. Fix for the value of variable \"a\"\n5. In sk_msg_shift_left, after shifting, i has already pointed to the next\nelement. Addtional sk_msg_iter_var_next may result in BUG."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
