            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56729",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: smb: Initialize cfid-\u003etcon before performing network ops"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: Initialize cfid-\u003etcon before performing network ops\n\nAvoid leaking a tcon ref when a lease break races with opening the\ncached directory. Processing the leak break might take a reference to\nthe tcon in cached_dir_lease_break() and then fail to release the ref in\ncached_dir_offload_close, since cfid-\u003etcon is still NULL."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56729",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56729\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56729](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56729)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: Initialize cfid-\u003etcon before performing network ops\n\nAvoid leaking a tcon ref when a lease break races with opening the\ncached directory. Processing the leak break might take a reference to\nthe tcon in cached_dir_lease_break() and then fail to release the ref in\ncached_dir_offload_close, since cfid-\u003etcon is still NULL.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56729**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56729](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56729)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: Initialize cfid-\u003etcon before performing network ops\n\nAvoid leaking a tcon ref when a lease break races with opening the\ncached directory. Processing the leak break might take a reference to\nthe tcon in cached_dir_lease_break() and then fail to release the ref in\ncached_dir_offload_close, since cfid-\u003etcon is still NULL."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56739",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: rtc: check if __rtc_read_time was successful in rtc_timer_do_work()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtc: check if __rtc_read_time was successful in rtc_timer_do_work()\n\nIf the __rtc_read_time call fails,, the struct rtc_time tm; may contain\nuninitialized data, or an illegal date/time read from the RTC hardware.\n\nWhen calling rtc_tm_to_ktime later, the result may be a very large value\n(possibly KTIME_MAX). If there are periodic timers in rtc-\u003etimerqueue,\nthey will continually expire, may causing kernel softlockup."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56739",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56739\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56739](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56739)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtc: check if __rtc_read_time was successful in rtc_timer_do_work()\n\nIf the __rtc_read_time call fails,, the struct rtc_time tm; may contain\nuninitialized data, or an illegal date/time read from the RTC hardware.\n\nWhen calling rtc_tm_to_ktime later, the result may be a very large value\n(possibly KTIME_MAX). If there are periodic timers in rtc-\u003etimerqueue,\nthey will continually expire, may causing kernel softlockup.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56739**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56739](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56739)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtc: check if __rtc_read_time was successful in rtc_timer_do_work()\n\nIf the __rtc_read_time call fails,, the struct rtc_time tm; may contain\nuninitialized data, or an illegal date/time read from the RTC hardware.\n\nWhen calling rtc_tm_to_ktime later, the result may be a very large value\n(possibly KTIME_MAX). If there are periodic timers in rtc-\u003etimerqueue,\nthey will continually expire, may causing kernel softlockup."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56742",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: vfio/mlx5: Fix an unwind issue in mlx5vf_add_migration_pages()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvfio/mlx5: Fix an unwind issue in mlx5vf_add_migration_pages()\n\nFix an unwind issue in mlx5vf_add_migration_pages().\n\nIf a set of pages is allocated but fails to be added to the SG table,\nthey need to be freed to prevent a memory leak.\n\nAny pages successfully added to the SG table will be freed as part of\nmlx5vf_free_data_buffer()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56742",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56742\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56742](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56742)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvfio/mlx5: Fix an unwind issue in mlx5vf_add_migration_pages()\n\nFix an unwind issue in mlx5vf_add_migration_pages().\n\nIf a set of pages is allocated but fails to be added to the SG table,\nthey need to be freed to prevent a memory leak.\n\nAny pages successfully added to the SG table will be freed as part of\nmlx5vf_free_data_buffer().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56742**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56742](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56742)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvfio/mlx5: Fix an unwind issue in mlx5vf_add_migration_pages()\n\nFix an unwind issue in mlx5vf_add_migration_pages().\n\nIf a set of pages is allocated but fails to be added to the SG table,\nthey need to be freed to prevent a memory leak.\n\nAny pages successfully added to the SG table will be freed as part of\nmlx5vf_free_data_buffer()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
