            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56745",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: PCI: Fix reset_method_store() memory leak"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: Fix reset_method_store() memory leak\n\nIn reset_method_store(), a string is allocated via kstrndup() and assigned\nto the local \"options\". options is then used in with strsep() to find\nspaces:\n\n  while ((name = strsep(\u0026options, \" \")) != NULL) {\n\nIf there are no remaining spaces, then options is set to NULL by strsep(),\nso the subsequent kfree(options) doesn't free the memory allocated via\nkstrndup().\n\nFix by using a separate tmp_options to iterate with strsep() so options is\npreserved."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56745",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56745\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56745](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56745)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: Fix reset_method_store() memory leak\n\nIn reset_method_store(), a string is allocated via kstrndup() and assigned\nto the local \"options\". options is then used in with strsep() to find\nspaces:\n\n  while ((name = strsep(\u0026options, \" \")) != NULL) {\n\nIf there are no remaining spaces, then options is set to NULL by strsep(),\nso the subsequent kfree(options) doesn't free the memory allocated via\nkstrndup().\n\nFix by using a separate tmp_options to iterate with strsep() so options is\npreserved.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56745**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56745](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56745)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: Fix reset_method_store() memory leak\n\nIn reset_method_store(), a string is allocated via kstrndup() and assigned\nto the local \"options\". options is then used in with strsep() to find\nspaces:\n\n  while ((name = strsep(\u0026options, \" \")) != NULL) {\n\nIf there are no remaining spaces, then options is set to NULL by strsep(),\nso the subsequent kfree(options) doesn't free the memory allocated via\nkstrndup().\n\nFix by using a separate tmp_options to iterate with strsep() so options is\npreserved."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56746",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: fbdev: sh7760fb: Fix a possible memory leak in sh7760fb_alloc_mem()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfbdev: sh7760fb: Fix a possible memory leak in sh7760fb_alloc_mem()\n\nWhen information such as info-\u003escreen_base is not ready, calling\nsh7760fb_free_mem() does not release memory correctly. Call\ndma_free_coherent() instead."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56746",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56746\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56746](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56746)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfbdev: sh7760fb: Fix a possible memory leak in sh7760fb_alloc_mem()\n\nWhen information such as info-\u003escreen_base is not ready, calling\nsh7760fb_free_mem() does not release memory correctly. Call\ndma_free_coherent() instead.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56746**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56746](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56746)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfbdev: sh7760fb: Fix a possible memory leak in sh7760fb_alloc_mem()\n\nWhen information such as info-\u003escreen_base is not ready, calling\nsh7760fb_free_mem() does not release memory correctly. Call\ndma_free_coherent() instead."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
