            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56763",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: tracing: Prevent bad count for tracing_cpumask_write"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing: Prevent bad count for tracing_cpumask_write\n\nIf a large count is provided, it will trigger a warning in bitmap_parse_user.\nAlso check zero for it."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56763",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56763\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-60.63\nLink: [CVE-2024-56763](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56763)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing: Prevent bad count for tracing_cpumask_write\n\nIf a large count is provided, it will trigger a warning in bitmap_parse_user.\nAlso check zero for it.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56763**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-60.63|[CVE-2024-56763](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56763)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntracing: Prevent bad count for tracing_cpumask_write\n\nIf a large count is provided, it will trigger a warning in bitmap_parse_user.\nAlso check zero for it."
              },
