            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-56782",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ACPI: x86: Add adev NULL check to acpi_quirk_skip_serdev_enumeration()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nACPI: x86: Add adev NULL check to acpi_quirk_skip_serdev_enumeration()\n\nacpi_dev_hid_match() does not check for adev == NULL, dereferencing\nit unconditional.\n\nAdd a check for adev being NULL before calling acpi_dev_hid_match().\n\nAt the moment acpi_quirk_skip_serdev_enumeration() is never called with\na controller_parent without an ACPI companion, but better safe than sorry."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56782",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-56782\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-56782](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56782)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nACPI: x86: Add adev NULL check to acpi_quirk_skip_serdev_enumeration()\n\nacpi_dev_hid_match() does not check for adev == NULL, dereferencing\nit unconditional.\n\nAdd a check for adev being NULL before calling acpi_dev_hid_match().\n\nAt the moment acpi_quirk_skip_serdev_enumeration() is never called with\na controller_parent without an ACPI companion, but better safe than sorry.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-56782**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-56782](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-56782)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nACPI: x86: Add adev NULL check to acpi_quirk_skip_serdev_enumeration()\n\nacpi_dev_hid_match() does not check for adev == NULL, dereferencing\nit unconditional.\n\nAdd a check for adev being NULL before calling acpi_dev_hid_match().\n\nAt the moment acpi_quirk_skip_serdev_enumeration() is never called with\na controller_parent without an ACPI companion, but better safe than sorry."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
