            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-57804",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: scsi: mpi3mr: Fix corrupt config pages PHY state is switched in sysfs"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: mpi3mr: Fix corrupt config pages PHY state is switched in sysfs\n\nThe driver, through the SAS transport, exposes a sysfs interface to\nenable/disable PHYs in a controller/expander setup.  When multiple PHYs\nare disabled and enabled in rapid succession, the persistent and current\nconfig pages related to SAS IO unit/SAS Expander pages could get\ncorrupted.\n\nUse separate memory for each config request."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57804",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-57804\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-60.63\nLink: [CVE-2024-57804](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57804)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: mpi3mr: Fix corrupt config pages PHY state is switched in sysfs\n\nThe driver, through the SAS transport, exposes a sysfs interface to\nenable/disable PHYs in a controller/expander setup.  When multiple PHYs\nare disabled and enabled in rapid succession, the persistent and current\nconfig pages related to SAS IO unit/SAS Expander pages could get\ncorrupted.\n\nUse separate memory for each config request.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-57804**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-60.63|[CVE-2024-57804](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57804)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: mpi3mr: Fix corrupt config pages PHY state is switched in sysfs\n\nThe driver, through the SAS transport, exposes a sysfs interface to\nenable/disable PHYs in a controller/expander setup.  When multiple PHYs\nare disabled and enabled in rapid succession, the persistent and current\nconfig pages related to SAS IO unit/SAS Expander pages could get\ncorrupted.\n\nUse separate memory for each config request."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
