            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-57807",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: scsi: megaraid_sas: Fix for a potential deadlock"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: megaraid_sas: Fix for a potential deadlock\n\nThis fixes a 'possible circular locking dependency detected' warning\n      CPU0                    CPU1\n      ----                    ----\n lock(\u0026instance-\u003ereset_mutex);\n                              lock(\u0026shost-\u003escan_mutex);\n                              lock(\u0026instance-\u003ereset_mutex);\n lock(\u0026shost-\u003escan_mutex);\n\nFix this by temporarily releasing the reset_mutex."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57807",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-57807\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-60.63\nLink: [CVE-2024-57807](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57807)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: megaraid_sas: Fix for a potential deadlock\n\nThis fixes a 'possible circular locking dependency detected' warning\n      CPU0                    CPU1\n      ----                    ----\n lock(\u0026instance-\u003ereset_mutex);\n                              lock(\u0026shost-\u003escan_mutex);\n                              lock(\u0026instance-\u003ereset_mutex);\n lock(\u0026shost-\u003escan_mutex);\n\nFix this by temporarily releasing the reset_mutex.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-57807**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-60.63|[CVE-2024-57807](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57807)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: megaraid_sas: Fix for a potential deadlock\n\nThis fixes a 'possible circular locking dependency detected' warning\n      CPU0                    CPU1\n      ----                    ----\n lock(\u0026instance-\u003ereset_mutex);\n                              lock(\u0026shost-\u003escan_mutex);\n                              lock(\u0026instance-\u003ereset_mutex);\n lock(\u0026shost-\u003escan_mutex);\n\nFix this by temporarily releasing the reset_mutex."
              },
