            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-57872",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: scsi: ufs: pltfrm: Dellocate HBA during ufshcd_pltfrm_remove()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: ufs: pltfrm: Dellocate HBA during ufshcd_pltfrm_remove()\n\nThis will ensure that the scsi host is cleaned up properly using\nscsi_host_dev_release(). Otherwise, it may lead to memory leaks."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57872",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-57872\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-58.60\nLink: [CVE-2024-57872](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57872)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: ufs: pltfrm: Dellocate HBA during ufshcd_pltfrm_remove()\n\nThis will ensure that the scsi host is cleaned up properly using\nscsi_host_dev_release(). Otherwise, it may lead to memory leaks.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-57872**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-58.60|[CVE-2024-57872](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57872)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: ufs: pltfrm: Dellocate HBA during ufshcd_pltfrm_remove()\n\nThis will ensure that the scsi host is cleaned up properly using\nscsi_host_dev_release(). Otherwise, it may lead to memory leaks."
              },
