            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-57879",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: Bluetooth: iso: Always release hdev at the end of iso_listen_bis"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: iso: Always release hdev at the end of iso_listen_bis\n\nSince hci_get_route holds the device before returning, the hdev\nshould be released with hci_dev_put at the end of iso_listen_bis\neven if the function returns with an error."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57879",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-57879\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-60.63\nLink: [CVE-2024-57879](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57879)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: iso: Always release hdev at the end of iso_listen_bis\n\nSince hci_get_route holds the device before returning, the hdev\nshould be released with hci_dev_put at the end of iso_listen_bis\neven if the function returns with an error.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-57879**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-60.63|[CVE-2024-57879](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57879)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: iso: Always release hdev at the end of iso_listen_bis\n\nSince hci_get_route holds the device before returning, the hdev\nshould be released with hci_dev_put at the end of iso_listen_bis\neven if the function returns with an error."
              },
