            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-57904",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: iio: adc: at91: call input_free_device() on allocated iio_dev"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: adc: at91: call input_free_device() on allocated iio_dev\n\nCurrent implementation of at91_ts_register() calls input_free_deivce()\non st-\u003ets_input, however, the err label can be reached before the\nallocated iio_dev is stored to st-\u003ets_input. Thus call\ninput_free_device() on input instead of st-\u003ets_input."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57904",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-57904\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-60.63\nLink: [CVE-2024-57904](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57904)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: adc: at91: call input_free_device() on allocated iio_dev\n\nCurrent implementation of at91_ts_register() calls input_free_deivce()\non st-\u003ets_input, however, the err label can be reached before the\nallocated iio_dev is stored to st-\u003ets_input. Thus call\ninput_free_device() on input instead of st-\u003ets_input.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-57904**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-60.63|[CVE-2024-57904](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57904)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: adc: at91: call input_free_device() on allocated iio_dev\n\nCurrent implementation of at91_ts_register() calls input_free_deivce()\non st-\u003ets_input, however, the err label can be reached before the\nallocated iio_dev is stored to st-\u003ets_input. Thus call\ninput_free_device() on input instead of st-\u003ets_input."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-57906",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: iio: adc: ti-ads8688: fix information leak in triggered buffer"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: adc: ti-ads8688: fix information leak in triggered buffer\n\nThe 'buffer' local array is used to push data to user space from a\ntriggered buffer, but it does not set values for inactive channels, as\nit only uses iio_for_each_active_channel() to assign new values.\n\nInitialize the array to zero before using it to avoid pushing\nuninitialized information to userspace."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57906",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-57906\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-60.63\nLink: [CVE-2024-57906](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57906)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: adc: ti-ads8688: fix information leak in triggered buffer\n\nThe 'buffer' local array is used to push data to user space from a\ntriggered buffer, but it does not set values for inactive channels, as\nit only uses iio_for_each_active_channel() to assign new values.\n\nInitialize the array to zero before using it to avoid pushing\nuninitialized information to userspace.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-57906**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-60.63|[CVE-2024-57906](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57906)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: adc: ti-ads8688: fix information leak in triggered buffer\n\nThe 'buffer' local array is used to push data to user space from a\ntriggered buffer, but it does not set values for inactive channels, as\nit only uses iio_for_each_active_channel() to assign new values.\n\nInitialize the array to zero before using it to avoid pushing\nuninitialized information to userspace."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
