            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-57931",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: selinux: ignore unknown extended permissions"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nselinux: ignore unknown extended permissions\n\nWhen evaluating extended permissions, ignore unknown permissions instead\nof calling BUG(). This commit ensures that future permissions can be\nadded without interfering with older kernels."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57931",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-57931\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-60.63\nLink: [CVE-2024-57931](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57931)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nselinux: ignore unknown extended permissions\n\nWhen evaluating extended permissions, ignore unknown permissions instead\nof calling BUG(). This commit ensures that future permissions can be\nadded without interfering with older kernels.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-57931**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-60.63|[CVE-2024-57931](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57931)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nselinux: ignore unknown extended permissions\n\nWhen evaluating extended permissions, ignore unknown permissions instead\nof calling BUG(). This commit ensures that future permissions can be\nadded without interfering with older kernels."
              },
              "properties": {
