            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-57938",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: net/sctp: Prevent autoclose integer overflow in sctp_association_init()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/sctp: Prevent autoclose integer overflow in sctp_association_init()\n\nWhile by default max_autoclose equals to INT_MAX / HZ, one may set\nnet.sctp.max_autoclose to UINT_MAX. There is code in\nsctp_association_init() that can consequently trigger overflow."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57938",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-57938\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-60.63\nLink: [CVE-2024-57938](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57938)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/sctp: Prevent autoclose integer overflow in sctp_association_init()\n\nWhile by default max_autoclose equals to INT_MAX / HZ, one may set\nnet.sctp.max_autoclose to UINT_MAX. There is code in\nsctp_association_init() that can consequently trigger overflow.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-57938**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-60.63|[CVE-2024-57938](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57938)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/sctp: Prevent autoclose integer overflow in sctp_association_init()\n\nWhile by default max_autoclose equals to INT_MAX / HZ, one may set\nnet.sctp.max_autoclose to UINT_MAX. There is code in\nsctp_association_init() that can consequently trigger overflow."
