            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-57940",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: exfat: fix the infinite loop in exfat_readdir()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nexfat: fix the infinite loop in exfat_readdir()\n\nIf the file system is corrupted so that a cluster is linked to\nitself in the cluster chain, and there is an unused directory\nentry in the cluster, 'dentry' will not be incremented, causing\ncondition 'dentry \u003c max_dentries' unable to prevent an infinite\nloop.\n\nThis infinite loop causes s_lock not to be released, and other\ntasks will hang, such as exfat_sync_fs().\n\nThis commit stops traversing the cluster chain when there is unused\ndirectory entry in the cluster to avoid this infinite loop."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57940",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-57940\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-60.63\nLink: [CVE-2024-57940](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57940)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nexfat: fix the infinite loop in exfat_readdir()\n\nIf the file system is corrupted so that a cluster is linked to\nitself in the cluster chain, and there is an unused directory\nentry in the cluster, 'dentry' will not be incremented, causing\ncondition 'dentry \u003c max_dentries' unable to prevent an infinite\nloop.\n\nThis infinite loop causes s_lock not to be released, and other\ntasks will hang, such as exfat_sync_fs().\n\nThis commit stops traversing the cluster chain when there is unused\ndirectory entry in the cluster to avoid this infinite loop.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-57940**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-60.63|[CVE-2024-57940](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57940)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nexfat: fix the infinite loop in exfat_readdir()\n\nIf the file system is corrupted so that a cluster is linked to\nitself in the cluster chain, and there is an unused directory\nentry in the cluster, 'dentry' will not be incremented, causing\ncondition 'dentry \u003c max_dentries' unable to prevent an infinite\nloop.\n\nThis infinite loop causes s_lock not to be released, and other\ntasks will hang, such as exfat_sync_fs().\n\nThis commit stops traversing the cluster chain when there is unused\ndirectory entry in the cluster to avoid this infinite loop."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
