            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-57973",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: rdma/cxgb4: Prevent potential integer overflow on 32bit"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrdma/cxgb4: Prevent potential integer overflow on 32bit\n\nThe \"gl-\u003etot_len\" variable is controlled by the user.  It comes from\nprocess_responses().  On 32bit systems, the \"gl-\u003etot_len + sizeof(struct\ncpl_pass_accept_req) + sizeof(struct rss_header)\" addition could have an\ninteger wrapping bug.  Use size_add() to prevent this."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57973",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-57973\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-64.67\nLink: [CVE-2024-57973](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57973)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrdma/cxgb4: Prevent potential integer overflow on 32bit\n\nThe \"gl-\u003etot_len\" variable is controlled by the user.  It comes from\nprocess_responses().  On 32bit systems, the \"gl-\u003etot_len + sizeof(struct\ncpl_pass_accept_req) + sizeof(struct rss_header)\" addition could have an\ninteger wrapping bug.  Use size_add() to prevent this.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-57973**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-64.67|[CVE-2024-57973](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-57973)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrdma/cxgb4: Prevent potential integer overflow on 32bit\n\nThe \"gl-\u003etot_len\" variable is controlled by the user.  It comes from\nprocess_responses().  On 32bit systems, the \"gl-\u003etot_len + sizeof(struct\ncpl_pass_accept_req) + sizeof(struct rss_header)\" addition could have an\ninteger wrapping bug.  Use size_add() to prevent this."
              },
