            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-58011",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: platform/x86: int3472: Check for adev == NULL"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/x86: int3472: Check for adev == NULL\n\nNot all devices have an ACPI companion fwnode, so adev might be NULL. This\ncan e.g. (theoretically) happen when a user manually binds one of\nthe int3472 drivers to another i2c/platform device through sysfs.\n\nAdd a check for adev not being set and return -ENODEV in that case to\navoid a possible NULL pointer deref in skl_int3472_get_acpi_buffer()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58011",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-58011\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-64.67\nLink: [CVE-2024-58011](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58011)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/x86: int3472: Check for adev == NULL\n\nNot all devices have an ACPI companion fwnode, so adev might be NULL. This\ncan e.g. (theoretically) happen when a user manually binds one of\nthe int3472 drivers to another i2c/platform device through sysfs.\n\nAdd a check for adev not being set and return -ENODEV in that case to\navoid a possible NULL pointer deref in skl_int3472_get_acpi_buffer().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-58011**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-64.67|[CVE-2024-58011](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58011)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/x86: int3472: Check for adev == NULL\n\nNot all devices have an ACPI companion fwnode, so adev might be NULL. This\ncan e.g. (theoretically) happen when a user manually binds one of\nthe int3472 drivers to another i2c/platform device through sysfs.\n\nAdd a check for adev not being set and return -ENODEV in that case to\navoid a possible NULL pointer deref in skl_int3472_get_acpi_buffer()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
