            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-58055",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: usb: gadget: f_tcm: Don't free command immediately"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: f_tcm: Don't free command immediately\n\nDon't prematurely free the command. Wait for the status completion of\nthe sense status. It can be freed then. Otherwise we will double-free\nthe command."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58055",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-58055\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-64.67\nLink: [CVE-2024-58055](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58055)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: f_tcm: Don't free command immediately\n\nDon't prematurely free the command. Wait for the status completion of\nthe sense status. It can be freed then. Otherwise we will double-free\nthe command.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-58055**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-64.67|[CVE-2024-58055](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58055)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: f_tcm: Don't free command immediately\n\nDon't prematurely free the command. Wait for the status completion of\nthe sense status. It can be freed then. Otherwise we will double-free\nthe command."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
