            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-58078",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: misc: misc_minor_alloc to use ida for all dynamic/misc dynamic minors"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmisc: misc_minor_alloc to use ida for all dynamic/misc dynamic minors\n\nmisc_minor_alloc was allocating id using ida for minor only in case of\nMISC_DYNAMIC_MINOR but misc_minor_free was always freeing ids\nusing ida_free causing a mismatch and following warn:\n\u003e \u003e WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 159 at lib/idr.c:525 ida_free+0x3e0/0x41f\n\u003e \u003e ida_free called for id=127 which is not allocated.\n\u003e \u003e \u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\n...\n\u003e \u003e [\u003c60941eb4\u003e] ida_free+0x3e0/0x41f\n\u003e \u003e [\u003c605ac993\u003e] misc_minor_free+0x3e/0xbc\n\u003e \u003e [\u003c605acb82\u003e] misc_deregister+0x171/0x1b3\n\nmisc_minor_alloc is changed to allocate id from ida for all minors\nfalling in the range of dynamic/ misc dynamic minors"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58078",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-58078\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-64.67\nLink: [CVE-2024-58078](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58078)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmisc: misc_minor_alloc to use ida for all dynamic/misc dynamic minors\n\nmisc_minor_alloc was allocating id using ida for minor only in case of\nMISC_DYNAMIC_MINOR but misc_minor_free was always freeing ids\nusing ida_free causing a mismatch and following warn:\n\u003e \u003e WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 159 at lib/idr.c:525 ida_free+0x3e0/0x41f\n\u003e \u003e ida_free called for id=127 which is not allocated.\n\u003e \u003e \u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\n...\n\u003e \u003e [\u003c60941eb4\u003e] ida_free+0x3e0/0x41f\n\u003e \u003e [\u003c605ac993\u003e] misc_minor_free+0x3e/0xbc\n\u003e \u003e [\u003c605acb82\u003e] misc_deregister+0x171/0x1b3\n\nmisc_minor_alloc is changed to allocate id from ida for all minors\nfalling in the range of dynamic/ misc dynamic minors",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-58078**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-64.67|[CVE-2024-58078](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2024-58078)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmisc: misc_minor_alloc to use ida for all dynamic/misc dynamic minors\n\nmisc_minor_alloc was allocating id using ida for minor only in case of\nMISC_DYNAMIC_MINOR but misc_minor_free was always freeing ids\nusing ida_free causing a mismatch and following warn:\n\u003e \u003e WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 159 at lib/idr.c:525 ida_free+0x3e0/0x41f\n\u003e \u003e ida_free called for id=127 which is not allocated.\n\u003e \u003e \u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\u003c\n...\n\u003e \u003e [\u003c60941eb4\u003e] ida_free+0x3e0/0x41f\n\u003e \u003e [\u003c605ac993\u003e] misc_minor_free+0x3e/0xbc\n\u003e \u003e [\u003c605acb82\u003e] misc_deregister+0x171/0x1b3\n\nmisc_minor_alloc is changed to allocate id from ida for all minors\nfalling in the range of dynamic/ misc dynamic minors"
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
