            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21659",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: netdev: prevent accessing NAPI instances from another namespace"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetdev: prevent accessing NAPI instances from another namespace\n\nThe NAPI IDs were not fully exposed to user space prior to the netlink\nAPI, so they were never namespaced. The netlink API must ensure that\nat the very least NAPI instance belongs to the same netns as the owner\nof the genl sock.\n\nnapi_by_id() can become static now, but it needs to move because of\ndev_get_by_napi_id()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21659",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21659\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-60.63\nLink: [CVE-2025-21659](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21659)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetdev: prevent accessing NAPI instances from another namespace\n\nThe NAPI IDs were not fully exposed to user space prior to the netlink\nAPI, so they were never namespaced. The netlink API must ensure that\nat the very least NAPI instance belongs to the same netns as the owner\nof the genl sock.\n\nnapi_by_id() can become static now, but it needs to move because of\ndev_get_by_napi_id().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21659**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-60.63|[CVE-2025-21659](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21659)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetdev: prevent accessing NAPI instances from another namespace\n\nThe NAPI IDs were not fully exposed to user space prior to the netlink\nAPI, so they were never namespaced. The netlink API must ensure that\nat the very least NAPI instance belongs to the same netns as the owner\nof the genl sock.\n\nnapi_by_id() can become static now, but it needs to move because of\ndev_get_by_napi_id()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21660",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ksmbd: fix unexpectedly changed path in ksmbd_vfs_kern_path_locked"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix unexpectedly changed path in ksmbd_vfs_kern_path_locked\n\nWhen `ksmbd_vfs_kern_path_locked` met an error and it is not the last\nentry, it will exit without restoring changed path buffer. But later this\nbuffer may be used as the filename for creation."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21660",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21660\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-60.63\nLink: [CVE-2025-21660](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21660)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix unexpectedly changed path in ksmbd_vfs_kern_path_locked\n\nWhen `ksmbd_vfs_kern_path_locked` met an error and it is not the last\nentry, it will exit without restoring changed path buffer. But later this\nbuffer may be used as the filename for creation.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21660**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-60.63|[CVE-2025-21660](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21660)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix unexpectedly changed path in ksmbd_vfs_kern_path_locked\n\nWhen `ksmbd_vfs_kern_path_locked` met an error and it is not the last\nentry, it will exit without restoring changed path buffer. But later this\nbuffer may be used as the filename for creation."
              },
              "properties": {
