            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21665",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: filemap: avoid truncating 64-bit offset to 32 bits"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfilemap: avoid truncating 64-bit offset to 32 bits\n\nOn 32-bit kernels, folio_seek_hole_data() was inadvertently truncating a\n64-bit value to 32 bits, leading to a possible infinite loop when writing\nto an xfs filesystem."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21665",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21665\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-62.65\nLink: [CVE-2025-21665](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21665)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfilemap: avoid truncating 64-bit offset to 32 bits\n\nOn 32-bit kernels, folio_seek_hole_data() was inadvertently truncating a\n64-bit value to 32 bits, leading to a possible infinite loop when writing\nto an xfs filesystem.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21665**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-62.65|[CVE-2025-21665](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21665)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfilemap: avoid truncating 64-bit offset to 32 bits\n\nOn 32-bit kernels, folio_seek_hole_data() was inadvertently truncating a\n64-bit value to 32 bits, leading to a possible infinite loop when writing\nto an xfs filesystem."
