            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21666",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: vsock: prevent null-ptr-deref in vsock_*[has_data|has_space]"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvsock: prevent null-ptr-deref in vsock_*[has_data|has_space]\n\nRecent reports have shown how we sometimes call vsock_*_has_data()\nwhen a vsock socket has been de-assigned from a transport (see attached\nlinks), but we shouldn't.\n\nPrevious commits should have solved the real problems, but we may have\nmore in the future, so to avoid null-ptr-deref, we can return 0\n(no space, no data available) but with a warning.\n\nThis way the code should continue to run in a nearly consistent state\nand have a warning that allows us to debug future problems."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21666",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21666\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-62.65\nLink: [CVE-2025-21666](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21666)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvsock: prevent null-ptr-deref in vsock_*[has_data|has_space]\n\nRecent reports have shown how we sometimes call vsock_*_has_data()\nwhen a vsock socket has been de-assigned from a transport (see attached\nlinks), but we shouldn't.\n\nPrevious commits should have solved the real problems, but we may have\nmore in the future, so to avoid null-ptr-deref, we can return 0\n(no space, no data available) but with a warning.\n\nThis way the code should continue to run in a nearly consistent state\nand have a warning that allows us to debug future problems.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21666**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-62.65|[CVE-2025-21666](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21666)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvsock: prevent null-ptr-deref in vsock_*[has_data|has_space]\n\nRecent reports have shown how we sometimes call vsock_*_has_data()\nwhen a vsock socket has been de-assigned from a transport (see attached\nlinks), but we shouldn't.\n\nPrevious commits should have solved the real problems, but we may have\nmore in the future, so to avoid null-ptr-deref, we can return 0\n(no space, no data available) but with a warning.\n\nThis way the code should continue to run in a nearly consistent state\nand have a warning that allows us to debug future problems."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
