            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21690",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: scsi: storvsc: Ratelimit warning logs to prevent VM denial of service"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: storvsc: Ratelimit warning logs to prevent VM denial of service\n\nIf there's a persistent error in the hypervisor, the SCSI warning for\nfailed I/O can flood the kernel log and max out CPU utilization,\npreventing troubleshooting from the VM side. Ratelimit the warning so\nit doesn't DoS the VM."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21690",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21690\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-62.65\nLink: [CVE-2025-21690](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21690)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: storvsc: Ratelimit warning logs to prevent VM denial of service\n\nIf there's a persistent error in the hypervisor, the SCSI warning for\nfailed I/O can flood the kernel log and max out CPU utilization,\npreventing troubleshooting from the VM side. Ratelimit the warning so\nit doesn't DoS the VM.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21690**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-62.65|[CVE-2025-21690](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21690)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: storvsc: Ratelimit warning logs to prevent VM denial of service\n\nIf there's a persistent error in the hypervisor, the SCSI warning for\nfailed I/O can flood the kernel log and max out CPU utilization,\npreventing troubleshooting from the VM side. Ratelimit the warning so\nit doesn't DoS the VM."
              },
              "properties": {
