            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21743",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: usbnet: ipheth: fix possible overflow in DPE length check"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusbnet: ipheth: fix possible overflow in DPE length check\n\nOriginally, it was possible for the DPE length check to overflow if\nwDatagramIndex + wDatagramLength \u003e U16_MAX. This could lead to an OoB\nread.\n\nMove the wDatagramIndex term to the other side of the inequality.\n\nAn existing condition ensures that wDatagramIndex \u003c urb-\u003eactual_length."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21743",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21743\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-64.67\nLink: [CVE-2025-21743](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21743)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusbnet: ipheth: fix possible overflow in DPE length check\n\nOriginally, it was possible for the DPE length check to overflow if\nwDatagramIndex + wDatagramLength \u003e U16_MAX. This could lead to an OoB\nread.\n\nMove the wDatagramIndex term to the other side of the inequality.\n\nAn existing condition ensures that wDatagramIndex \u003c urb-\u003eactual_length.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21743**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-64.67|[CVE-2025-21743](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21743)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusbnet: ipheth: fix possible overflow in DPE length check\n\nOriginally, it was possible for the DPE length check to overflow if\nwDatagramIndex + wDatagramLength \u003e U16_MAX. This could lead to an OoB\nread.\n\nMove the wDatagramIndex term to the other side of the inequality.\n\nAn existing condition ensures that wDatagramIndex \u003c urb-\u003eactual_length."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21744",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: wifi: brcmfmac: fix NULL pointer dereference in brcmf_txfinalize()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: brcmfmac: fix NULL pointer dereference in brcmf_txfinalize()\n\nOn removal of the device or unloading of the kernel module a potential NULL\npointer dereference occurs.\n\nThe following sequence deletes the interface:\n\n  brcmf_detach()\n    brcmf_remove_interface()\n      brcmf_del_if()\n\nInside the brcmf_del_if() function the drvr-\u003eif2bss[ifidx] is updated to\nBRCMF_BSSIDX_INVALID (-1) if the bsscfgidx matches.\n\nAfter brcmf_remove_interface() call the brcmf_proto_detach() function is\ncalled providing the following sequence:\n\n  brcmf_detach()\n    brcmf_proto_detach()\n      brcmf_proto_msgbuf_detach()\n        brcmf_flowring_detach()\n          brcmf_msgbuf_delete_flowring()\n            brcmf_msgbuf_remove_flowring()\n              brcmf_flowring_delete()\n                brcmf_get_ifp()\n                brcmf_txfinalize()\n\nSince brcmf_get_ip() can and actually will return NULL in this case the\ncall to brcmf_txfinalize() will result in a NULL pointer dereference inside\nbrcmf_txfinalize() when trying to update ifp-\u003endev-\u003estats.tx_errors.\n\nThis will only happen if a flowring still has an skb.\n\nAlthough the NULL pointer dereference has only been seen when trying to\nupdate the tx statistic, all other uses of the ifp pointer have been\nguarded as well with an early return if ifp is NULL."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21744",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21744\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-64.67\nLink: [CVE-2025-21744](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21744)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: brcmfmac: fix NULL pointer dereference in brcmf_txfinalize()\n\nOn removal of the device or unloading of the kernel module a potential NULL\npointer dereference occurs.\n\nThe following sequence deletes the interface:\n\n  brcmf_detach()\n    brcmf_remove_interface()\n      brcmf_del_if()\n\nInside the brcmf_del_if() function the drvr-\u003eif2bss[ifidx] is updated to\nBRCMF_BSSIDX_INVALID (-1) if the bsscfgidx matches.\n\nAfter brcmf_remove_interface() call the brcmf_proto_detach() function is\ncalled providing the following sequence:\n\n  brcmf_detach()\n    brcmf_proto_detach()\n      brcmf_proto_msgbuf_detach()\n        brcmf_flowring_detach()\n          brcmf_msgbuf_delete_flowring()\n            brcmf_msgbuf_remove_flowring()\n              brcmf_flowring_delete()\n                brcmf_get_ifp()\n                brcmf_txfinalize()\n\nSince brcmf_get_ip() can and actually will return NULL in this case the\ncall to brcmf_txfinalize() will result in a NULL pointer dereference inside\nbrcmf_txfinalize() when trying to update ifp-\u003endev-\u003estats.tx_errors.\n\nThis will only happen if a flowring still has an skb.\n\nAlthough the NULL pointer dereference has only been seen when trying to\nupdate the tx statistic, all other uses of the ifp pointer have been\nguarded as well with an early return if ifp is NULL.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21744**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-64.67|[CVE-2025-21744](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21744)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: brcmfmac: fix NULL pointer dereference in brcmf_txfinalize()\n\nOn removal of the device or unloading of the kernel module a potential NULL\npointer dereference occurs.\n\nThe following sequence deletes the interface:\n\n  brcmf_detach()\n    brcmf_remove_interface()\n      brcmf_del_if()\n\nInside the brcmf_del_if() function the drvr-\u003eif2bss[ifidx] is updated to\nBRCMF_BSSIDX_INVALID (-1) if the bsscfgidx matches.\n\nAfter brcmf_remove_interface() call the brcmf_proto_detach() function is\ncalled providing the following sequence:\n\n  brcmf_detach()\n    brcmf_proto_detach()\n      brcmf_proto_msgbuf_detach()\n        brcmf_flowring_detach()\n          brcmf_msgbuf_delete_flowring()\n            brcmf_msgbuf_remove_flowring()\n              brcmf_flowring_delete()\n                brcmf_get_ifp()\n                brcmf_txfinalize()\n\nSince brcmf_get_ip() can and actually will return NULL in this case the\ncall to brcmf_txfinalize() will result in a NULL pointer dereference inside\nbrcmf_txfinalize() when trying to update ifp-\u003endev-\u003estats.tx_errors.\n\nThis will only happen if a flowring still has an skb.\n\nAlthough the NULL pointer dereference has only been seen when trying to\nupdate the tx statistic, all other uses of the ifp pointer have been\nguarded as well with an early return if ifp is NULL."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21745",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: blk-cgroup: Fix class @block_class's subsystem refcount leakage"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nblk-cgroup: Fix class @block_class's subsystem refcount leakage\n\nblkcg_fill_root_iostats() iterates over @block_class's devices by\nclass_dev_iter_(init|next)(), but does not end iterating with\nclass_dev_iter_exit(), so causes the class's subsystem refcount leakage.\n\nFix by ending the iterating with class_dev_iter_exit()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21745",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21745\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-64.67\nLink: [CVE-2025-21745](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21745)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nblk-cgroup: Fix class @block_class's subsystem refcount leakage\n\nblkcg_fill_root_iostats() iterates over @block_class's devices by\nclass_dev_iter_(init|next)(), but does not end iterating with\nclass_dev_iter_exit(), so causes the class's subsystem refcount leakage.\n\nFix by ending the iterating with class_dev_iter_exit().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21745**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-64.67|[CVE-2025-21745](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21745)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nblk-cgroup: Fix class @block_class's subsystem refcount leakage\n\nblkcg_fill_root_iostats() iterates over @block_class's devices by\nclass_dev_iter_(init|next)(), but does not end iterating with\nclass_dev_iter_exit(), so causes the class's subsystem refcount leakage.\n\nFix by ending the iterating with class_dev_iter_exit()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21746",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: Input: synaptics - fix crash when enabling pass-through port"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nInput: synaptics - fix crash when enabling pass-through port\n\nWhen enabling a pass-through port an interrupt might come before psmouse\ndriver binds to the pass-through port. However synaptics sub-driver\ntries to access psmouse instance presumably associated with the\npass-through port to figure out if only 1 byte of response or entire\nprotocol packet needs to be forwarded to the pass-through port and may\ncrash if psmouse instance has not been attached to the port yet.\n\nFix the crash by introducing open() and close() methods for the port and\ncheck if the port is open before trying to access psmouse instance.\nBecause psmouse calls serio_open() only after attaching psmouse instance\nto serio port instance this prevents the potential crash."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21746",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21746\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-78.78\nLink: [CVE-2025-21746](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21746)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nInput: synaptics - fix crash when enabling pass-through port\n\nWhen enabling a pass-through port an interrupt might come before psmouse\ndriver binds to the pass-through port. However synaptics sub-driver\ntries to access psmouse instance presumably associated with the\npass-through port to figure out if only 1 byte of response or entire\nprotocol packet needs to be forwarded to the pass-through port and may\ncrash if psmouse instance has not been attached to the port yet.\n\nFix the crash by introducing open() and close() methods for the port and\ncheck if the port is open before trying to access psmouse instance.\nBecause psmouse calls serio_open() only after attaching psmouse instance\nto serio port instance this prevents the potential crash.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21746**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-78.78|[CVE-2025-21746](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21746)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nInput: synaptics - fix crash when enabling pass-through port\n\nWhen enabling a pass-through port an interrupt might come before psmouse\ndriver binds to the pass-through port. However synaptics sub-driver\ntries to access psmouse instance presumably associated with the\npass-through port to figure out if only 1 byte of response or entire\nprotocol packet needs to be forwarded to the pass-through port and may\ncrash if psmouse instance has not been attached to the port yet.\n\nFix the crash by introducing open() and close() methods for the port and\ncheck if the port is open before trying to access psmouse instance.\nBecause psmouse calls serio_open() only after attaching psmouse instance\nto serio port instance this prevents the potential crash."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21748",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ksmbd: fix integer overflows on 32 bit systems"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix integer overflows on 32 bit systems\n\nOn 32bit systems the addition operations in ipc_msg_alloc() can\npotentially overflow leading to memory corruption.\nAdd bounds checking using KSMBD_IPC_MAX_PAYLOAD to avoid overflow."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21748",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21748\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-64.67\nLink: [CVE-2025-21748](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21748)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix integer overflows on 32 bit systems\n\nOn 32bit systems the addition operations in ipc_msg_alloc() can\npotentially overflow leading to memory corruption.\nAdd bounds checking using KSMBD_IPC_MAX_PAYLOAD to avoid overflow.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21748**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-64.67|[CVE-2025-21748](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21748)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix integer overflows on 32 bit systems\n\nOn 32bit systems the addition operations in ipc_msg_alloc() can\npotentially overflow leading to memory corruption.\nAdd bounds checking using KSMBD_IPC_MAX_PAYLOAD to avoid overflow."
              },
