              "id": "CVE-2025-21749",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: net: rose: lock the socket in rose_bind()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: rose: lock the socket in rose_bind()\n\nsyzbot reported a soft lockup in rose_loopback_timer(),\nwith a repro calling bind() from multiple threads.\n\nrose_bind() must lock the socket to avoid this issue."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21749",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21749\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-64.67\nLink: [CVE-2025-21749](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21749)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: rose: lock the socket in rose_bind()\n\nsyzbot reported a soft lockup in rose_loopback_timer(),\nwith a repro calling bind() from multiple threads.\n\nrose_bind() must lock the socket to avoid this issue.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21749**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-64.67|[CVE-2025-21749](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21749)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: rose: lock the socket in rose_bind()\n\nsyzbot reported a soft lockup in rose_loopback_timer(),\nwith a repro calling bind() from multiple threads.\n\nrose_bind() must lock the socket to avoid this issue."
