            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21759",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ipv6: mcast: extend RCU protection in igmp6_send()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv6: mcast: extend RCU protection in igmp6_send()\n\nigmp6_send() can be called without RTNL or RCU being held.\n\nExtend RCU protection so that we can safely fetch the net pointer\nand avoid a potential UAF.\n\nNote that we no longer can use sock_alloc_send_skb() because\nipv6.igmp_sk uses GFP_KERNEL allocations which can sleep.\n\nInstead use alloc_skb() and charge the net-\u003eipv6.igmp_sk\nsocket under RCU protection."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21759",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21759\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-78.78\nLink: [CVE-2025-21759](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21759)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv6: mcast: extend RCU protection in igmp6_send()\n\nigmp6_send() can be called without RTNL or RCU being held.\n\nExtend RCU protection so that we can safely fetch the net pointer\nand avoid a potential UAF.\n\nNote that we no longer can use sock_alloc_send_skb() because\nipv6.igmp_sk uses GFP_KERNEL allocations which can sleep.\n\nInstead use alloc_skb() and charge the net-\u003eipv6.igmp_sk\nsocket under RCU protection.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21759**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-78.78|[CVE-2025-21759](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21759)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv6: mcast: extend RCU protection in igmp6_send()\n\nigmp6_send() can be called without RTNL or RCU being held.\n\nExtend RCU protection so that we can safely fetch the net pointer\nand avoid a potential UAF.\n\nNote that we no longer can use sock_alloc_send_skb() because\nipv6.igmp_sk uses GFP_KERNEL allocations which can sleep.\n\nInstead use alloc_skb() and charge the net-\u003eipv6.igmp_sk\nsocket under RCU protection."
              },
