            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21793",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: spi: sn-f-ospi: Fix division by zero"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nspi: sn-f-ospi: Fix division by zero\n\nWhen there is no dummy cycle in the spi-nor commands, both dummy bus cycle\nbytes and width are zero. Because of the cpu's warning when divided by\nzero, the warning should be avoided. Return just zero to avoid such\ncalculations."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21793",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21793\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-78.78\nLink: [CVE-2025-21793](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21793)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nspi: sn-f-ospi: Fix division by zero\n\nWhen there is no dummy cycle in the spi-nor commands, both dummy bus cycle\nbytes and width are zero. Because of the cpu's warning when divided by\nzero, the warning should be avoided. Return just zero to avoid such\ncalculations.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21793**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-78.78|[CVE-2025-21793](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21793)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nspi: sn-f-ospi: Fix division by zero\n\nWhen there is no dummy cycle in the spi-nor commands, both dummy bus cycle\nbytes and width are zero. Because of the cpu's warning when divided by\nzero, the warning should be avoided. Return just zero to avoid such\ncalculations."
              },
              "properties": {
