            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21838",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: usb: gadget: core: flush gadget workqueue after device removal"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: core: flush gadget workqueue after device removal\n\ndevice_del() can lead to new work being scheduled in gadget-\u003ework\nworkqueue. This is observed, for example, with the dwc3 driver with the\nfollowing call stack:\n  device_del()\n    gadget_unbind_driver()\n      usb_gadget_disconnect_locked()\n        dwc3_gadget_pullup()\n\t  dwc3_gadget_soft_disconnect()\n\t    usb_gadget_set_state()\n\t      schedule_work(\u0026gadget-\u003ework)\n\nMove flush_work() after device_del() to ensure the workqueue is cleaned\nup."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21838",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21838\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-78.78\nLink: [CVE-2025-21838](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21838)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: core: flush gadget workqueue after device removal\n\ndevice_del() can lead to new work being scheduled in gadget-\u003ework\nworkqueue. This is observed, for example, with the dwc3 driver with the\nfollowing call stack:\n  device_del()\n    gadget_unbind_driver()\n      usb_gadget_disconnect_locked()\n        dwc3_gadget_pullup()\n\t  dwc3_gadget_soft_disconnect()\n\t    usb_gadget_set_state()\n\t      schedule_work(\u0026gadget-\u003ework)\n\nMove flush_work() after device_del() to ensure the workqueue is cleaned\nup.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21838**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-78.78|[CVE-2025-21838](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21838)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: gadget: core: flush gadget workqueue after device removal\n\ndevice_del() can lead to new work being scheduled in gadget-\u003ework\nworkqueue. This is observed, for example, with the dwc3 driver with the\nfollowing call stack:\n  device_del()\n    gadget_unbind_driver()\n      usb_gadget_disconnect_locked()\n        dwc3_gadget_pullup()\n\t  dwc3_gadget_soft_disconnect()\n\t    usb_gadget_set_state()\n\t      schedule_work(\u0026gadget-\u003ework)\n\nMove flush_work() after device_del() to ensure the workqueue is cleaned\nup."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
