            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21844",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: smb: client: Add check for next_buffer in receive_encrypted_standard()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: Add check for next_buffer in receive_encrypted_standard()\n\nAdd check for the return value of cifs_buf_get() and cifs_small_buf_get()\nin receive_encrypted_standard() to prevent null pointer dereference."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21844",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21844\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-78.78\nLink: [CVE-2025-21844](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21844)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: Add check for next_buffer in receive_encrypted_standard()\n\nAdd check for the return value of cifs_buf_get() and cifs_small_buf_get()\nin receive_encrypted_standard() to prevent null pointer dereference.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21844**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-78.78|[CVE-2025-21844](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21844)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: Add check for next_buffer in receive_encrypted_standard()\n\nAdd check for the return value of cifs_buf_get() and cifs_small_buf_get()\nin receive_encrypted_standard() to prevent null pointer dereference."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
