              "id": "CVE-2025-21863",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: io_uring: prevent opcode speculation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nio_uring: prevent opcode speculation\n\nsqe-\u003eopcode is used for different tables, make sure we santitise it\nagainst speculations."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21863",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21863\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-78.78\nLink: [CVE-2025-21863](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21863)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nio_uring: prevent opcode speculation\n\nsqe-\u003eopcode is used for different tables, make sure we santitise it\nagainst speculations.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21863**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-78.78|[CVE-2025-21863](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21863)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nio_uring: prevent opcode speculation\n\nsqe-\u003eopcode is used for different tables, make sure we santitise it\nagainst speculations."
