            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21945",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ksmbd: fix use-after-free in smb2_lock"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix use-after-free in smb2_lock\n\nIf smb_lock-\u003ezero_len has value, -\u003ellist of smb_lock is not delete and\nflock is old one. It will cause use-after-free on error handling\nroutine."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21945",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21945\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-84.84\nLink: [CVE-2025-21945](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21945)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix use-after-free in smb2_lock\n\nIf smb_lock-\u003ezero_len has value, -\u003ellist of smb_lock is not delete and\nflock is old one. It will cause use-after-free on error handling\nroutine.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21945**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-84.84|[CVE-2025-21945](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21945)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix use-after-free in smb2_lock\n\nIf smb_lock-\u003ezero_len has value, -\u003ellist of smb_lock is not delete and\nflock is old one. It will cause use-after-free on error handling\nroutine."
