            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21967",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ksmbd: fix use-after-free in ksmbd_free_work_struct"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix use-after-free in ksmbd_free_work_struct\n\n-\u003einterim_entry of ksmbd_work could be deleted after oplock is freed.\nWe don't need to manage it with linked list. The interim request could be\nimmediately sent whenever a oplock break wait is needed."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21967",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21967\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-84.84\nLink: [CVE-2025-21967](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21967)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix use-after-free in ksmbd_free_work_struct\n\n-\u003einterim_entry of ksmbd_work could be deleted after oplock is freed.\nWe don't need to manage it with linked list. The interim request could be\nimmediately sent whenever a oplock break wait is needed.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21967**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-84.84|[CVE-2025-21967](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21967)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix use-after-free in ksmbd_free_work_struct\n\n-\u003einterim_entry of ksmbd_work could be deleted after oplock is freed.\nWe don't need to manage it with linked list. The interim request could be\nimmediately sent whenever a oplock break wait is needed."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
