            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21971",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: net_sched: Prevent creation of classes with TC_H_ROOT"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet_sched: Prevent creation of classes with TC_H_ROOT\n\nThe function qdisc_tree_reduce_backlog() uses TC_H_ROOT as a termination\ncondition when traversing up the qdisc tree to update parent backlog\ncounters. However, if a class is created with classid TC_H_ROOT, the\ntraversal terminates prematurely at this class instead of reaching the\nactual root qdisc, causing parent statistics to be incorrectly maintained.\nIn case of DRR, this could lead to a crash as reported by Mingi Cho.\n\nPrevent the creation of any Qdisc class with classid TC_H_ROOT\n(0xFFFFFFFF) across all qdisc types, as suggested by Jamal."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21971",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21971\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-60.63\nLink: [CVE-2025-21971](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21971)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet_sched: Prevent creation of classes with TC_H_ROOT\n\nThe function qdisc_tree_reduce_backlog() uses TC_H_ROOT as a termination\ncondition when traversing up the qdisc tree to update parent backlog\ncounters. However, if a class is created with classid TC_H_ROOT, the\ntraversal terminates prematurely at this class instead of reaching the\nactual root qdisc, causing parent statistics to be incorrectly maintained.\nIn case of DRR, this could lead to a crash as reported by Mingi Cho.\n\nPrevent the creation of any Qdisc class with classid TC_H_ROOT\n(0xFFFFFFFF) across all qdisc types, as suggested by Jamal.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21971**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-60.63|[CVE-2025-21971](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21971)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet_sched: Prevent creation of classes with TC_H_ROOT\n\nThe function qdisc_tree_reduce_backlog() uses TC_H_ROOT as a termination\ncondition when traversing up the qdisc tree to update parent backlog\ncounters. However, if a class is created with classid TC_H_ROOT, the\ntraversal terminates prematurely at this class instead of reaching the\nactual root qdisc, causing parent statistics to be incorrectly maintained.\nIn case of DRR, this could lead to a crash as reported by Mingi Cho.\n\nPrevent the creation of any Qdisc class with classid TC_H_ROOT\n(0xFFFFFFFF) across all qdisc types, as suggested by Jamal."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21972",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: net: mctp: unshare packets when reassembling"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: mctp: unshare packets when reassembling\n\nEnsure that the frag_list used for reassembly isn't shared with other\npackets. This avoids incorrect reassembly when packets are cloned, and\nprevents a memory leak due to circular references between fragments and\ntheir skb_shared_info.\n\nThe upcoming MCTP-over-USB driver uses skb_clone which can trigger the\nproblem - other MCTP drivers don't share SKBs.\n\nA kunit test is added to reproduce the issue."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21972",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21972\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-84.84\nLink: [CVE-2025-21972](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21972)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: mctp: unshare packets when reassembling\n\nEnsure that the frag_list used for reassembly isn't shared with other\npackets. This avoids incorrect reassembly when packets are cloned, and\nprevents a memory leak due to circular references between fragments and\ntheir skb_shared_info.\n\nThe upcoming MCTP-over-USB driver uses skb_clone which can trigger the\nproblem - other MCTP drivers don't share SKBs.\n\nA kunit test is added to reproduce the issue.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21972**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-84.84|[CVE-2025-21972](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21972)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: mctp: unshare packets when reassembling\n\nEnsure that the frag_list used for reassembly isn't shared with other\npackets. This avoids incorrect reassembly when packets are cloned, and\nprevents a memory leak due to circular references between fragments and\ntheir skb_shared_info.\n\nThe upcoming MCTP-over-USB driver uses skb_clone which can trigger the\nproblem - other MCTP drivers don't share SKBs.\n\nA kunit test is added to reproduce the issue."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21975",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: net/mlx5: handle errors in mlx5_chains_create_table()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/mlx5: handle errors in mlx5_chains_create_table()\n\nIn mlx5_chains_create_table(), the return value of mlx5_get_fdb_sub_ns()\nand mlx5_get_flow_namespace() must be checked to prevent NULL pointer\ndereferences. If either function fails, the function should log error\nmessage with mlx5_core_warn() and return error pointer."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21975",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21975\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-84.84\nLink: [CVE-2025-21975](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21975)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/mlx5: handle errors in mlx5_chains_create_table()\n\nIn mlx5_chains_create_table(), the return value of mlx5_get_fdb_sub_ns()\nand mlx5_get_flow_namespace() must be checked to prevent NULL pointer\ndereferences. If either function fails, the function should log error\nmessage with mlx5_core_warn() and return error pointer.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21975**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-84.84|[CVE-2025-21975](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21975)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/mlx5: handle errors in mlx5_chains_create_table()\n\nIn mlx5_chains_create_table(), the return value of mlx5_get_fdb_sub_ns()\nand mlx5_get_flow_namespace() must be checked to prevent NULL pointer\ndereferences. If either function fails, the function should log error\nmessage with mlx5_core_warn() and return error pointer."
              },
