            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21980",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: sched: address a potential NULL pointer dereference in the GRED scheduler."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsched: address a potential NULL pointer dereference in the GRED scheduler.\n\nIf kzalloc in gred_init returns a NULL pointer, the code follows the\nerror handling path, invoking gred_destroy. This, in turn, calls\ngred_offload, where memset could receive a NULL pointer as input,\npotentially leading to a kernel crash.\n\nWhen table-\u003eopt is NULL in gred_init(), gred_change_table_def()\nis not called yet, so it is not necessary to call -\u003endo_setup_tc()\nin gred_offload()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21980",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21980\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-84.84\nLink: [CVE-2025-21980](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21980)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsched: address a potential NULL pointer dereference in the GRED scheduler.\n\nIf kzalloc in gred_init returns a NULL pointer, the code follows the\nerror handling path, invoking gred_destroy. This, in turn, calls\ngred_offload, where memset could receive a NULL pointer as input,\npotentially leading to a kernel crash.\n\nWhen table-\u003eopt is NULL in gred_init(), gred_change_table_def()\nis not called yet, so it is not necessary to call -\u003endo_setup_tc()\nin gred_offload().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21980**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-84.84|[CVE-2025-21980](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21980)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsched: address a potential NULL pointer dereference in the GRED scheduler.\n\nIf kzalloc in gred_init returns a NULL pointer, the code follows the\nerror handling path, invoking gred_destroy. This, in turn, calls\ngred_offload, where memset could receive a NULL pointer as input,\npotentially leading to a kernel crash.\n\nWhen table-\u003eopt is NULL in gred_init(), gred_change_table_def()\nis not called yet, so it is not necessary to call -\u003endo_setup_tc()\nin gred_offload()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
