            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21994",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ksmbd: fix incorrect validation for num_aces field of smb_acl"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix incorrect validation for num_aces field of smb_acl\n\nparse_dcal() validate num_aces to allocate posix_ace_state_array.\n\nif (num_aces \u003e ULONG_MAX / sizeof(struct smb_ace *))\n\nIt is an incorrect validation that we can create an array of size ULONG_MAX.\nsmb_acl has -\u003esize field to calculate actual number of aces in request buffer\nsize. Use this to check invalid num_aces."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21994",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21994\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-84.84\nLink: [CVE-2025-21994](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21994)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix incorrect validation for num_aces field of smb_acl\n\nparse_dcal() validate num_aces to allocate posix_ace_state_array.\n\nif (num_aces \u003e ULONG_MAX / sizeof(struct smb_ace *))\n\nIt is an incorrect validation that we can create an array of size ULONG_MAX.\nsmb_acl has -\u003esize field to calculate actual number of aces in request buffer\nsize. Use this to check invalid num_aces.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21994**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-84.84|[CVE-2025-21994](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21994)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix incorrect validation for num_aces field of smb_acl\n\nparse_dcal() validate num_aces to allocate posix_ace_state_array.\n\nif (num_aces \u003e ULONG_MAX / sizeof(struct smb_ace *))\n\nIt is an incorrect validation that we can create an array of size ULONG_MAX.\nsmb_acl has -\u003esize field to calculate actual number of aces in request buffer\nsize. Use this to check invalid num_aces."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
