            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-21995",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: drm/sched: Fix fence reference count leak"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/sched: Fix fence reference count leak\n\nThe last_scheduled fence leaks when an entity is being killed and adding\nthe cleanup callback fails.\n\nDecrement the reference count of prev when dma_fence_add_callback()\nfails, ensuring proper balance.\n\n[phasta: add git tag info for stable kernel]"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21995",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-21995\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-84.84\nLink: [CVE-2025-21995](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21995)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/sched: Fix fence reference count leak\n\nThe last_scheduled fence leaks when an entity is being killed and adding\nthe cleanup callback fails.\n\nDecrement the reference count of prev when dma_fence_add_callback()\nfails, ensuring proper balance.\n\n[phasta: add git tag info for stable kernel]",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-21995**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-84.84|[CVE-2025-21995](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-21995)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/sched: Fix fence reference count leak\n\nThe last_scheduled fence leaks when an entity is being killed and adding\nthe cleanup callback fails.\n\nDecrement the reference count of prev when dma_fence_add_callback()\nfails, ensuring proper balance.\n\n[phasta: add git tag info for stable kernel]"
              },
