            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-22039",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ksmbd: fix overflow in dacloffset bounds check"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix overflow in dacloffset bounds check\n\nThe dacloffset field was originally typed as int and used in an\nunchecked addition, which could overflow and bypass the existing\nbounds check in both smb_check_perm_dacl() and smb_inherit_dacl().\n\nThis could result in out-of-bounds memory access and a kernel crash\nwhen dereferencing the DACL pointer.\n\nThis patch converts dacloffset to unsigned int and uses\ncheck_add_overflow() to validate access to the DACL."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22039",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-22039\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-86.87\nLink: [CVE-2025-22039](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22039)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix overflow in dacloffset bounds check\n\nThe dacloffset field was originally typed as int and used in an\nunchecked addition, which could overflow and bypass the existing\nbounds check in both smb_check_perm_dacl() and smb_inherit_dacl().\n\nThis could result in out-of-bounds memory access and a kernel crash\nwhen dereferencing the DACL pointer.\n\nThis patch converts dacloffset to unsigned int and uses\ncheck_add_overflow() to validate access to the DACL.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-22039**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-86.87|[CVE-2025-22039](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22039)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix overflow in dacloffset bounds check\n\nThe dacloffset field was originally typed as int and used in an\nunchecked addition, which could overflow and bypass the existing\nbounds check in both smb_check_perm_dacl() and smb_inherit_dacl().\n\nThis could result in out-of-bounds memory access and a kernel crash\nwhen dereferencing the DACL pointer.\n\nThis patch converts dacloffset to unsigned int and uses\ncheck_add_overflow() to validate access to the DACL."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-22040",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ksmbd: fix session use-after-free in multichannel connection"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix session use-after-free in multichannel connection\n\nThere is a race condition between session setup and\nksmbd_sessions_deregister. The session can be freed before the connection\nis added to channel list of session.\nThis patch check reference count of session before freeing it."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22040",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-22040\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-86.87\nLink: [CVE-2025-22040](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22040)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix session use-after-free in multichannel connection\n\nThere is a race condition between session setup and\nksmbd_sessions_deregister. The session can be freed before the connection\nis added to channel list of session.\nThis patch check reference count of session before freeing it.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-22040**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-86.87|[CVE-2025-22040](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22040)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix session use-after-free in multichannel connection\n\nThere is a race condition between session setup and\nksmbd_sessions_deregister. The session can be freed before the connection\nis added to channel list of session.\nThis patch check reference count of session before freeing it."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
