            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-22041",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ksmbd: fix use-after-free in ksmbd_sessions_deregister()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix use-after-free in ksmbd_sessions_deregister()\n\nIn multichannel mode, UAF issue can occur in session_deregister\nwhen the second channel sets up a session through the connection of\nthe first channel. session that is freed through the global session\ntable can be accessed again through -\u003esessions of connection."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22041",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-22041\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-86.87\nLink: [CVE-2025-22041](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22041)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix use-after-free in ksmbd_sessions_deregister()\n\nIn multichannel mode, UAF issue can occur in session_deregister\nwhen the second channel sets up a session through the connection of\nthe first channel. session that is freed through the global session\ntable can be accessed again through -\u003esessions of connection.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-22041**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-86.87|[CVE-2025-22041](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-22041)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix use-after-free in ksmbd_sessions_deregister()\n\nIn multichannel mode, UAF issue can occur in session_deregister\nwhen the second channel sets up a session through the connection of\nthe first channel. session that is freed through the global session\ntable can be accessed again through -\u003esessions of connection."
              },
