            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-37838",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: HSI: ssi_protocol: Fix use after free vulnerability in ssi_protocol Driver Due to Race Condition"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHSI: ssi_protocol: Fix use after free vulnerability in ssi_protocol Driver Due to Race Condition\n\nIn the ssi_protocol_probe() function, \u0026ssi-\u003ework is bound with\nssip_xmit_work(), In ssip_pn_setup(), the ssip_pn_xmit() function\nwithin the ssip_pn_ops structure is capable of starting the\nwork.\n\nIf we remove the module which will call ssi_protocol_remove()\nto make a cleanup, it will free ssi through kfree(ssi),\nwhile the work mentioned above will be used. The sequence\nof operations that may lead to a UAF bug is as follows:\n\nCPU0                                    CPU1\n\n                        | ssip_xmit_work\nssi_protocol_remove     |\nkfree(ssi);             |\n                        | struct hsi_client *cl = ssi-\u003ecl;\n                        | // use ssi\n\nFix it by ensuring that the work is canceled before proceeding\nwith the cleanup in ssi_protocol_remove()."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-37838",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-37838\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-87.88\nLink: [CVE-2025-37838](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-37838)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHSI: ssi_protocol: Fix use after free vulnerability in ssi_protocol Driver Due to Race Condition\n\nIn the ssi_protocol_probe() function, \u0026ssi-\u003ework is bound with\nssip_xmit_work(), In ssip_pn_setup(), the ssip_pn_xmit() function\nwithin the ssip_pn_ops structure is capable of starting the\nwork.\n\nIf we remove the module which will call ssi_protocol_remove()\nto make a cleanup, it will free ssi through kfree(ssi),\nwhile the work mentioned above will be used. The sequence\nof operations that may lead to a UAF bug is as follows:\n\nCPU0                                    CPU1\n\n                        | ssip_xmit_work\nssi_protocol_remove     |\nkfree(ssi);             |\n                        | struct hsi_client *cl = ssi-\u003ecl;\n                        | // use ssi\n\nFix it by ensuring that the work is canceled before proceeding\nwith the cleanup in ssi_protocol_remove().",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-37838**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-87.88|[CVE-2025-37838](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-37838)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHSI: ssi_protocol: Fix use after free vulnerability in ssi_protocol Driver Due to Race Condition\n\nIn the ssi_protocol_probe() function, \u0026ssi-\u003ework is bound with\nssip_xmit_work(), In ssip_pn_setup(), the ssip_pn_xmit() function\nwithin the ssip_pn_ops structure is capable of starting the\nwork.\n\nIf we remove the module which will call ssi_protocol_remove()\nto make a cleanup, it will free ssi through kfree(ssi),\nwhile the work mentioned above will be used. The sequence\nof operations that may lead to a UAF bug is as follows:\n\nCPU0                                    CPU1\n\n                        | ssip_xmit_work\nssi_protocol_remove     |\nkfree(ssi);             |\n                        | struct hsi_client *cl = ssi-\u003ecl;\n                        | // use ssi\n\nFix it by ensuring that the work is canceled before proceeding\nwith the cleanup in ssi_protocol_remove()."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
