            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-38575",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: ksmbd: use aead_request_free to match aead_request_alloc"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: use aead_request_free to match aead_request_alloc\n\nUse aead_request_free() instead of kfree() to properly free memory\nallocated by aead_request_alloc(). This ensures sensitive crypto data\nis zeroed before being freed."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-38575",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-38575\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-86.87\nLink: [CVE-2025-38575](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-38575)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: use aead_request_free to match aead_request_alloc\n\nUse aead_request_free() instead of kfree() to properly free memory\nallocated by aead_request_alloc(). This ensures sensitive crypto data\nis zeroed before being freed.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-38575**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-86.87|[CVE-2025-38575](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-38575)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: use aead_request_free to match aead_request_alloc\n\nUse aead_request_free() instead of kfree() to properly free memory\nallocated by aead_request_alloc(). This ensures sensitive crypto data\nis zeroed before being freed."
              },
