            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-39728",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: clk: samsung: Fix UBSAN panic in samsung_clk_init()"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nclk: samsung: Fix UBSAN panic in samsung_clk_init()\n\nWith UBSAN_ARRAY_BOUNDS=y, I'm hitting the below panic due to\ndereferencing `ctx-\u003eclk_data.hws` before setting\n`ctx-\u003eclk_data.num = nr_clks`. Move that up to fix the crash.\n\n  UBSAN: array index out of bounds: 00000000f2005512 [#1] PREEMPT SMP\n  \u003csnip\u003e\n  Call trace:\n   samsung_clk_init+0x110/0x124 (P)\n   samsung_clk_init+0x48/0x124 (L)\n   samsung_cmu_register_one+0x3c/0xa0\n   exynos_arm64_register_cmu+0x54/0x64\n   __gs101_cmu_top_of_clk_init_declare+0x28/0x60\n   ..."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-39728",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-39728\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-86.87\nLink: [CVE-2025-39728](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-39728)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nclk: samsung: Fix UBSAN panic in samsung_clk_init()\n\nWith UBSAN_ARRAY_BOUNDS=y, I'm hitting the below panic due to\ndereferencing `ctx-\u003eclk_data.hws` before setting\n`ctx-\u003eclk_data.num = nr_clks`. Move that up to fix the crash.\n\n  UBSAN: array index out of bounds: 00000000f2005512 [#1] PREEMPT SMP\n  \u003csnip\u003e\n  Call trace:\n   samsung_clk_init+0x110/0x124 (P)\n   samsung_clk_init+0x48/0x124 (L)\n   samsung_cmu_register_one+0x3c/0xa0\n   exynos_arm64_register_cmu+0x54/0x64\n   __gs101_cmu_top_of_clk_init_declare+0x28/0x60\n   ...",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-39728**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-86.87|[CVE-2025-39728](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-39728)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nclk: samsung: Fix UBSAN panic in samsung_clk_init()\n\nWith UBSAN_ARRAY_BOUNDS=y, I'm hitting the below panic due to\ndereferencing `ctx-\u003eclk_data.hws` before setting\n`ctx-\u003eclk_data.num = nr_clks`. Move that up to fix the crash.\n\n  UBSAN: array index out of bounds: 00000000f2005512 [#1] PREEMPT SMP\n  \u003csnip\u003e\n  Call trace:\n   samsung_clk_init+0x110/0x124 (P)\n   samsung_clk_init+0x48/0x124 (L)\n   samsung_cmu_register_one+0x3c/0xa0\n   exynos_arm64_register_cmu+0x54/0x64\n   __gs101_cmu_top_of_clk_init_declare+0x28/0x60\n   ..."
              },
