            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-39964",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: crypto: af_alg - Disallow concurrent writes in af_alg_sendmsg"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: af_alg - Disallow concurrent writes in af_alg_sendmsg\n\nIssuing two writes to the same af_alg socket is bogus as the\ndata will be interleaved in an unpredictable fashion.  Furthermore,\nconcurrent writes may create inconsistencies in the internal\nsocket state.\n\nDisallow this by adding a new ctx-\u003ewrite field that indiciates\nexclusive ownership for writing."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-39964",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-39964\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-90.91\nLink: [CVE-2025-39964](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-39964)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: af_alg - Disallow concurrent writes in af_alg_sendmsg\n\nIssuing two writes to the same af_alg socket is bogus as the\ndata will be interleaved in an unpredictable fashion.  Furthermore,\nconcurrent writes may create inconsistencies in the internal\nsocket state.\n\nDisallow this by adding a new ctx-\u003ewrite field that indiciates\nexclusive ownership for writing.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-39964**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-90.91|[CVE-2025-39964](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-39964)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: af_alg - Disallow concurrent writes in af_alg_sendmsg\n\nIssuing two writes to the same af_alg socket is bogus as the\ndata will be interleaved in an unpredictable fashion.  Furthermore,\nconcurrent writes may create inconsistencies in the internal\nsocket state.\n\nDisallow this by adding a new ctx-\u003ewrite field that indiciates\nexclusive ownership for writing."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
