            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-40364",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kernel: io_uring: fix io_req_prep_async with provided buffers"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nio_uring: fix io_req_prep_async with provided buffers\n\nio_req_prep_async() can import provided buffers, commit the ring state\nby giving up on that before, it'll be reimported later if needed."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40364",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-40364\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: linux-libc-dev\nFixed Version: 6.8.0-64.67\nLink: [CVE-2025-40364](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40364)\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nio_uring: fix io_req_prep_async with provided buffers\n\nio_req_prep_async() can import provided buffers, commit the ring state\nby giving up on that before, it'll be reimported later if needed.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-40364**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|linux-libc-dev|6.8.0-64.67|[CVE-2025-40364](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-40364)|\n\nIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nio_uring: fix io_req_prep_async with provided buffers\n\nio_req_prep_async() can import provided buffers, commit the ring state\nby giving up on that before, it'll be reimported later if needed."
