            {
              "id": "CVE-2019-16775",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "npm: Symlink reference outside of node_modules folder through the bin field upon installation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Versions of the npm CLI prior to 6.13.3 are vulnerable to an Arbitrary File Write. It is possible for packages to create symlinks to files outside of thenode_modules folder through the bin field upon installation. A properly constructed entry in the package.json bin field would allow a package publisher to create a symlink pointing to arbitrary files on a user's system when the package is installed. This behavior is still possible through install scripts. This vulnerability bypasses a user using the --ignore-scripts install option."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-16775",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2019-16775\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: npm\nFixed Version: 6.13.3\nLink: [CVE-2019-16775](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-16775)\nVersions of the npm CLI prior to 6.13.3 are vulnerable to an Arbitrary File Write. It is possible for packages to create symlinks to files outside of thenode_modules folder through the bin field upon installation. A properly constructed entry in the package.json bin field would allow a package publisher to create a symlink pointing to arbitrary files on a user's system when the package is installed. This behavior is still possible through install scripts. This vulnerability bypasses a user using the --ignore-scripts install option.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2019-16775**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|npm|6.13.3|[CVE-2019-16775](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-16775)|\n\nVersions of the npm CLI prior to 6.13.3 are vulnerable to an Arbitrary File Write. It is possible for packages to create symlinks to files outside of thenode_modules folder through the bin field upon installation. A properly constructed entry in the package.json bin field would allow a package publisher to create a symlink pointing to arbitrary files on a user's system when the package is installed. This behavior is still possible through install scripts. This vulnerability bypasses a user using the --ignore-scripts install option."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 7.7,
